AB  -  INTERVENTION: Test group:From 10 min before anesthesia induction, the Test group was given transcutaneous electrical stimulation at bilateral Ququan, Taichong, Yinlingquan and Sanyinjiao acupoints until the end of the operation. The electrical stimulator was set as alternating density wave with frequency of 2 / 100 Hz, and the current intensity was the maximum intensity that the child could tolerate ( 10‐15 mA ). In addition, the same acupoints were continuously stimulated by transcutaneous electrical acupoint stimulation on the 1st‐3rd day after operation, and the density wave was alternately stimulated at 2 / 100 Hz for 3 s, lasting for 30 min, once a day.;Control group:In the control group, electrode tablets were pasted on the same acupoints from 10 min before anesthesia induction and 1‐3 days after operation, but no electrical stimulation was given to inform the children that the new treatment had no sensation.; CONDITION: Diseases of the penis in children PRIMARY OUTCOME: Pain scores; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Changes of peripheral blood stress hormone levels and pain‐related substances levels; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1)Meet the diagnosis of penile‐related diseases in children including prepuce phimosis cryptorchid penis etc.; 2) Children aged 5‐18 years old; 3) ASA grading I‐II; 4) Normal intelligence can communicate; 5) Obtain permission from the child and his/her family.
