AB  -  INTERVENTION: Study Group:On the basis of providing routine care to the participants of the mixed hemorrhoids study, TEAS was immediately administered after the completion of the surgical handover. The selected acupoints were Chengshan (both sides), Zusanli (both sides), Hegu (both sides), Changqiang, and Zhongji. The operation method: Adjust the frequency of the low‐frequency pulse therapy device, place the electrode patches on the selected acupoints, and provide continuous transcutaneous electrical acupoint stimulation for pain relief. The current intensity was set at the maximum tolerable level acceptable to the participants. Each session lasted for 20 minutes, once a day, for a total of 3 days.;Control group:After the completion of surgical handover, the participants in the mixed hemorrhoid study were immediately given routine care. The participants after surgery used the visual analogue scale (VAS) to score = 4 points, and were given oral copifen for pain relief. If the participants still felt severe pain 1 hour after taking the medication and could not tolerate it, additional medication could be taken, with a daily dose not exceeding 5 tablets. During the treatment period, other pain‐relieving drugs were stopped, and the dosage of pain medication for the participants was recorded. The treatment course was 3 days.; CONDITION: mixed hemorrhoids PRIMARY OUTCOME: Postoperative anal pain score; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Postoperative perianal edema score;Postoperative bleeding score;Wound healing time;Patient hospitalization expenses;The length of the patient's hospital stay;Patient treatment satisfaction;The occurrence of adverse reactions during the patient's treatment; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Patients with stage III ‐ IV mixed hemorrhoids who are scheduled for elective surgical treatment; (2) Aged between 18 and 65 years old; (3) Having civil capacity; (4) Having normal structure and function of the lower digestive tract such as the anus and rectum; (5) Being able to cooperate with the inquiry of medical history, physical and specialized examinations, and understand and fill out the survey forms; (6) Signing the surgical and informed consent forms, having good compliance, and being willing to accept the treatment plan.
