AB  -  INTERVENTION: Treatment group:1. Acupoints: Jianzhong (GB39) on the healthy side, Sanyinjiao (SP6), and Biyuan (ST31). 2. Equipment: SDZ‐II Electroacupuncture Device (Suzhou Medical Devices Co., Ltd., Suzhou Medical Device Registration Approval Number) 20172200675) (2/100 Hz, sparse‐dense waves, =10 mA). 2. 3. Timing: Stimulate for 30 minutes prior to surgery on the 1st hour of the Shen period (15:00–17:00). During the procedure (30 minutes before anesthesia to the end of the surgery) and for 1‐3 days post‐surgery, apply stimulation at the noon hour (15:00 – 17:00) for 30 minutes each day. 4. Intensity adjustment: To a level where there is localized muscle micro‐tremors and the patient can tolerate a tolerable sensation of acidity and swelling.;Control group:1. Acupoints: Same as the experimental group. 2. Equipment and Parameters: The device used is identical in appearance, sound, and operational procedures to the experimental group. Specific equipment with parameters set to extremely low output intensity (= 1 mA) and no mode selected. Microcurrents with specific therapeutic significance. 3. Timing and Process: Exactly the same as the experimental group.; CONDITION: Hip fracture PRIMARY OUTCOME: Post‐operative recovery quality; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Post‐operative recovery quality;Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Inde X(PSQI) score;Initial venting/time to get out of bed;Rest/Exercise(visual analogue scale, VAS)rating;Number of PCIA pressure applications;Adjunct analgesic dosage;Preoperative and postoperative 24 hours white blood cell count;Incidence of nausea and vomiting;Incidence of deep vein thrombosis;Incidence of lung infections;Local skin reaction;Total length of hospital stay;Length of stay in the ICU; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Patients aged 65 or older undergoing elective hip fracture surgery (2) ASA Grade II‐III (3) Voluntarily participate in the trial and sign an informed consent form
