AB  -  INTERVENTION: Medical Device : All treatments will be carried out by Korean Medicine Doctors with over 2 years of clinical experience and in accordance with predefined protocol and Standard Operating Procedures. A total of 4 treatments will be performed. 1 hour pre‐operation and 1 hour post‐operation treatments will be performed on the day of the surgery(Day 0). On the day after surgery(Day 1), one treatment will be carried out in the morning(08:30‐12:00) and another in the afternoon(14:30‐18:00) with at least 4 hours of time difference in between. The EA and sham EA are both performed in same sites and both groups will undergo same post‐operative analgesics intervention. CONDITION: Diseases of the digestive system PRIMARY OUTCOME: 11‐point pain intensity numerical rating scale (PI‐NRS) SECONDARY OUTCOME: 11‐point pain intensity numerical rating scale (PI‐NRS) 11‐point PI‐NRS (intensity of nausea, vomiting, disorientation, itching) 11‐point PI‐NRS (post‐laparoscopic surgery shoulder pain) Adverse events Blinding test Quality of life (EQ‐5D) Total amount of pain medication used INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1) Males and females aged 19 to 65 years 2) Diagnosed with appendicitis and scheduled for laparoscopic appendectomy 3) Provided with explanation regarding the purpose and characteristics of this study and agreed to written informed consent
