AB  -  INTERVENTION: Transcutaneous auricular vagus nerve stimulation group:Accept bilateral TEAS auricular internal organ area/auricle area, with normal instrumentation for stimulation. Interventions are carried out at 2h, 24h, 48h, and 72h post‐operation. The electrical stimulation parameters are a frequency of 25Hz, current of 3mA, and duration of 30 minutes. Monitor patient responses and vital signs, gradually increasing the stimulation current to 3mA within 5 minutes.;Sham Transcutaneous Vagus Nerve Stimulation Group:Subjects assigned to the ShamTEAS auricular acupoint group will receive sham stimulation, with the stimulation device being a placebo stimulator. The stimulation duration and stimulation parameters are set to be the same as those in the TEAS auricular acupoint group.; CONDITION: postoperative ileus after Radical Gastrectomy PRIMARY OUTCOME: First exhaust time; SECONDARY OUTCOME: First bowel movement time;The incidence of POI extension;Timing of water intake ;Liquid diet tolerance time;Solid food tolerance time;Number of episodes of nausea, vomiting, and bloating;Severity of postoperative pain;First out‐of‐bed time;First independent walking time;Length of postoperative hospital stay;Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS‐2002);Quality of Life Questionnaire;Adverse events (AEs);Severe complications; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Pathologically diagnosed gastric cancer (stage I‐III), American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) grade I‐III, and planned to undergo elective laparoscopic gastrectomy; (2) Age: 18‐75 years old, gender is not limited; (3) Patients who voluntarily or their families agree to participate in the trial and sign the informed consent form for the trial.
