AB  -  Objectives: To explore the clinical results of hot compress with Chinese materia medica evodia on the abdomen in combination with electro‐acupuncture at the point of Zusanli (ST 36) for the intestinal function recovery after post‐operative colorectal cancer. Methods: 112 cases with colorectal canceer were randomly divided into the observation group and the control group, each group for 56 cases. Patients of two groups both received the conventional nursing of surgery department. And the observation group received the hot compress on the abdomen with Chinese materia medica evodia combined with electro‐acupuncture at the point of Zusanli (ST 36). Results: patients in the observation group quickly recover the intestinal function. And the time of anal aerofluxus and abdominal distention was shorten, which is better than the control group (P<0.01). Conclusion: The traditional Chinese medicine nursing intervention ‐‐ hot compress with Chinese materia medica evodia on the abdomen associated with electro‐accupuncture at the point of Zusanli (ST 36) can remarkably reduce the time of anal aerofluxus and defecation after the operation, improve the dysfunction of gastrointestinal motility, and promote the recovery the gastrointestinal function. Besides, it also has the important significance in preventing serious complication of anastomotic leakage, intestinal adhesive and intestinal ileus.
