AB  -  INTERVENTION: TEAS group:The electrodes were attached to both Hegu points, Neiguan points, Lixie points and Qiuze points of the patient, connected to the electrical stimulator, and the parameters were set as follows: density wave, frequency 2/100 Hz, current intensity 10 mA, time for 30 min.;Sham TEAS group:The electrodes were attached to the same acupuncture points as the TEAS group, and the electrical stimulator with the same appearance as the TEAS group was connected, but no power was applied, and the device was maintained for 30 min.; CONDITION: Difficult airway PRIMARY OUTCOME: Heart rate and mean arterial pressure; SECONDARY OUTCOME: BIS;Ramsay sedation score;SpO2; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Patients undergoing nasal tracheal intubation guided by awake fiberbronchoscope; 2. American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Grade I to III; 3. Age 18‐70 years old; 4. The patient volunteered and signed the informed consent.
