AB  -  INTERVENTION: Study Group:Participants in the study were administered TEAS immediately after completing surgical handover, in addition to standard care protocols. Acupoints selected: Zhongji (CV12), Guanyuan (CV4), Qihai (CV6), Shuidao (CV12, unilateral), and Sanyinjiao (SP6, bilateral). Procedure method: Adjust the frequency of the low‐frequency pulse therapy device, place the electrode patch on the percutaneous acupoints, and perform continuous percutaneous electrical stimulation for analgesia. The current intensity was determined based on the maximum tolerable level of the participants. The treatment was administered once daily for 20 minutes each session, over a period of 3 days.;Control group:In addition to standard nursing care, study participants were instructed on how to urinate in bed or by the bedside, such as listening to the sound of running water. A conducive environment for urination was provided, and participants were guided to rela Xand follow their usual urination habits to alleviate or eliminate tension caused by urination. Appropriate abdominal compression was recommended during urination.; CONDITION: mixed hemorrhoids PRIMARY OUTCOME: Postoperative incidence of urinary retention;The time of the first spontaneous urination after the operation;The volume of urine during the first urination after the operation;Residual urine volume after the first postoperative spontaneous urination ;Postoperative first urination score; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Postoperative anal pain score;Postoperative perianal edema score;Wound healing time;Patient hospitalization expenses;The length of the patient's hospital stay;Patient treatment satisfaction;The occurrence of adverse reactions during the patient's treatment; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Patients with mixed hemorrhoids (Grade III–IV) scheduled for elective surgery; 2. Aged 18–65 years; 3. Possess legal capacity; 4. Have normal structure and function of the lower gastrointestinal tract, including the anorectal region; 5. Are able to cooperate with medical history interviews, physical examinations, and specialized tests, and can understand and complete survey forms; 6. Have signed the surgical and informed consent forms, demonstrate good compliance, and are willing to accept the treatment plan.
