AB  -  INTERVENTION: Experimental group:On the postoperative day, electronic acupuncture therapy apparatus (Huatuo card, SDZ‐V type) was used to stimulate acupoints including Neiguan (PC 6), Hegu (LI 4), Zusanli (ST 36) and Sanyinjiao (SP 6). The pulse current, disperse‐dense wave, frequency of 2Hz/100Hz, and current intensity of 6‐15mA were selected. Pulse current, dense and sparse waves were selected, with a frequency of 2Hz/100Hz, and the current intensity ranging from 6 to 15mA. The optimal current intensity was adjusted to maintain a slight twitch of the local muscles, based on the patients maximum tolerance. The stimulation lasted for 30 minutes each time. On the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd days after the surgery, the stimulation positions and parameters were the same as before, with each stimulation lasting for 30 minutes per time, once a day. The stimulation time was 30min. The stimulation position and parameters were the same as before at 1, 2 and 3 days after operation, 30min each time, once a day.;Control group:Pseudo‐percutaneous acupoint electrical stimulation treatment; CONDITION: Postpartum depression PRIMARY OUTCOME: Edinburghpostnataldepression scale ;Social Support Rating Scale;Time to first flatus;Time to first defecation;Time to first oral intake ; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Numerical Rating Scale point;Athens Insomnia Scale point; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. A singleton full‐term pregnant woman scheduled for elective cesarean section under spinal anesthesia; 2. ASA II‐III grade; 3. Age >= 20 years old; 4. Clearly understand and voluntarily participate in this study, and sign the informed consent form by oneself.
