AB  -  INTERVENTION: Group A: control group (Sham TEAS + saline) :30 minutes before induction of anesthesia, 1 day and 2 days after operation, the dominant side of Neiguan and He were selected. Sham TEAS ( target acupoint electrode patch, but no stimulation ) was performed on " tuogu " and " zusanli " points for 30 minutes, and 1 ml of normal saline was injected intravenously 30 minutes before the end of the operation.; Group B: drug group (Sham TEAS + metoclopramide):30 minutes before induction of anesthesia, 1 day and 2 days after operation, the dominant side of Neiguan and He were selected. Sham TEAS ( target acupoint electrode patch, but no stimulation ) was performed at Gu and Zusanli for 30 min. Metoclopramide 10 mg was injected intravenously 30 min before the end of the operation.;Group C: combination group (TEAS + metoclopramide):30 minutes before induction of anesthesia, 1 day and 2 days after operation, the dominant side of Neiguan and He were selected. TEAS was performed at Gu and Zusanli for 30 min, and 10 mg metoclopramide was injected intravenously 30 min before the end of the operation. TEAS was set at a frequency of 2 / 100 Hz, and the electrical stimulation intensity was based on the patient 's maximum tolerance. According to the patient 's tolerance, it was set to 2‐3 times of the sensory threshold, generally set between 6‐20 mA.; CONDITION: Uterine fibroids, adenomyosis, endometriosis PRIMARY OUTCOME: The incidence of postoperative nausea and vomiting within 24 hours after operation;Adverse events (treatment related/unrelated); SECONDARY OUTCOME: The incidence of PON, POV, PONV and severity of nausea and the number of vomiting/dry heaves were recorded for 0‐2h, 2‐6h, 6‐24h, and 24‐48h postoperatively.;Postoperative pain VAS scores, use of remedial antiemetic (ondansetron) versus opioids during the 48h postoperative period were recorded, and patient satisfaction was assessed after 48h postoperatively.;The operation time, anesthesia time, extubation time, recovery time, total hospital stay, intraoperative propofol dosage, remifentanil dosage, intraoperative bleeding, and fluid infusion were recorded.;Basic patient information was recorded: age, height, weight, BMI, smoking history, history of motion sickness/PONV, and type of surgery.; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1: Patients undergoing elective gynecological laparoscopic surgery 2: Age : 18‐65 years 3: BMI:18 .5‐28Kg / m^2 4: ASA grade I‐II 5: Signing informed consent
