TI  -  Forty cases of chronic lumbar muscle strain treated with electro-acupuncture on Huatuo Jiaji point
JA  -  Henan traditional chinese medicine [henan zhong yi]
PY  -  2015
VL  -  35
IS  -  8
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  1866‐1868
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objectives: To observe the clinical curative effect of electro‐acupuncture on Huatuo Jiaji point (EX‐B2) on chronic lumbar muscle strain. Methods: Eighty patients with chronic lumbar muscle strain were randomly divided into the observation group and control group, with 40 cases in each group. The ones in the observation group were given electro‐acupuncture on Huatuo Jiaji point, while the ones in the control group were given electro‐acupuncture on Shenshu (BL 23), Dachangshu (BL 25) and Guanyuanshu (BL 26) on both sides of the body. Results: The effective rate of the observation group was 97.5%, while that of the control group was 90.0%; And the differences between them had statistical significance (X2=4.029, P<0.05). After the treatment, ODI level and VAS level of both groups decreased obviously (P<0.01); And the decreased degree of the observation group was much better than those of the control group (P<0.01). Conclusion: Electro‐acupuncture on Huatuo Jiaji point has remarkable clinical curative effect on chronic lumbar muscle strain with exact points, few side‐effects and simple operation.
UR  -  https://www.cochranelibrary.com/central/doi/10.1002/central/CN-01436682/full
ER  -  


