AB  -  INTERVENTION: Drug group:Take oral flunarizine hydrochloride capsules, 10 mg each time, once a day, before going to bed every night. Continue the treatment for 2 weeks.;15‐minute electroacupuncture group:. The patient lies on their back, with the acupuncture site exposed. The operator presses on the acupuncture point to identify the point of pain response. The site is then disinfected with 75% alcohol. The operator selects a 0.25 mm × 40 mm or 0.25 mm × 25 mm single‐use Huatuo brand sterile acupuncture needle. The points Guanyu, Tianwei, Baihui, and Sun are inserted downward at a depth of 8‐15 mm; Fengchi is inserted obliquely towards the tip of the nose at a depth of 15‐25 mm; when inserting Guanyu, the patient holds their hand in a half‐clenched fist, and the needle is inserted straight at a depth of 12‐20 mm; Sanyingjiao is inserted straight at a depth of 10‐15 mm. The lifting, inserting, and twisting techniques are used to allow the needle to penetrate and gain qi. For the two groups of acupuncture points, namely Tianwei and Guanyu, Fengchi and Sun, the Han‐style electro‐acupuncture machine is used. The frequency is 2/100Hz, and the intensity is adjusted according to the patients tolerance. The needle is retained for 15 minutes with electricity, and then removed after the electro‐acupuncture is completed. Treatment schedule: Treatment is given once every other day, three times a week, for a total of two weeks as one treatment course. After 8 weeks, a follow‐up visit is conducted.;30‐minute electro‐acupuncture group:30‐minute electro‐acupuncture group: The needles are left in and energized for 30 minutes, and then the needles are removed after the electro‐acupuncture session is completed. The acupuncture points, operation procedures, treatment course, and follow‐up visits are all CONDITION: migraine PRIMARY OUTCOME: Cerebral hemodynamic indicators;5‐HT; SECONDARY OUTCOME: short‐form of McGill pain questionnaire, SF‐MPQ;Hamilton depression rating scale;Total score of TCM syndromes; INCLUSION CRITERIA: INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Meet the above diagnostic criteria of migraine without aura; 2. Both sexes, aged between 18 and 65 years old; 3. Migraine attack frequency at least once every 3 months; 4, the effect of drugs and other treatment methods is not obvious or recurrent; 5. Discontinue other migraine drugs without aura for at least 1 week before treatment.
