AB  -  Objective: To observe the clinical effect of external application of Chinese medicine on umbilicus combined with electro‐acupuncture for treating overactive bladder syndrome (OAB) after transurethral resection of prostate (TURF). Methods: Collected 83 cases patients with OAB after TURP in clinic and randomized into combined‐treatment group 42 cases and control group 41 cases. Combined treatment group were treated with external application of Chinese medicine on umbilicus from the day of operation, hot compress 3 times per day, 30 min every time, combined with electro‐acupuncture on Guanyuan (BL 26), Shenshu (BL 23), Pangguangshu (BL 28), Xialiao (BL 34) for 30 min, 1 time per day, for 2 weeks. Control group were treated with oral administration toherodine 2mg from the day of operation, twice per day, for 2 weeks. Compared number of times of cystospasm with pain in the catheter period after TURP, times of duration, urine volume of every time in automatic micturition period, number of times of urge urinary incontinence, average urgent urination of every day, OABSS assessment scores of 2 groups. Results: Number of times and duration of cystospasm with pain in the catheter period after TURP of combined‐treatment group were less than that of control group; In automatic micturition period, number of times of urge urinary incontinence, average urgent urination of every day, OABSS assessment scores of combined‐treatment group were all less than that of control group while index like urine volume of every time were better than that of control group (P<0.05). Conclusion: Clinical effect of external application of Chinese medicine on umbilicus combined with electro‐acupuncture for treating overactive bladder syndrome (OAB) after transurethral resection of prostate (TURF) is significant and had relatively high safety.
