AB  -  INTERVENTION: Procedure/Surgery : A study that compares treatment efficacy of electro‐acupuncture (EA) VS sham electro‐acupuncture (S‐EA) VS usual care in the treatment of mild cognitive impairment. Treatment regimen: 2 times/week for 12 weeks (for EA / S‐EA group) Follow period: 12 weeks after treatment completion CONDITION: Mental and behavioral disorders PRIMARY OUTCOME: Seoul Neuropsychological Screening Battery (SNSB) SECONDARY OUTCOME: Adverse events Alzheimer's disease assessment scale cognitive subscale (ADAS‐Cog) Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS) Korean Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA‐K) Patient Global Impression of Change INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. aged from equal to or more than 45 to under 80 years old 2. Patients who meet the Peterson diagnostic criteria of mild cognitive impairment (MCI) with memory problems at least for 3 months 3. clinical dementia rating score 0.5 AND global deterioration scale score 2‐3 4. Hachinski ischemic score = 4 5. at least 6 years of education 6. agreed with written informed consent
