AB  -  Hypochondriac Pain is a disease with the clinical manifestation of one side or both sides chest pain, and it is a common clinical auto psyche symptoms. Cholelithiasis is a surgical disease, one of the most important clinical manifestations is chest pain. Clinical treatment of paining in the Western medicine is using the drugs in acute pain relief, it has lotsof side effects and high cost, many patients could not bear it. In recent years, Acupuncture did a lot of work on in‐depth study of Paining, it provide the basis to the treatment and a deep understanding of such diseases. Acupuncture showing great potential and advantages in reducing the patient suffering, the side effects of western medicine, and the cost of treatment and so on, it has become increasingly accepted. Combined with the clinical experience and comprehensive study of ancient literature, I have 60 patients, who were the Hypochondriac Pain Cause by Cholelithiasis, studied under the guidance of instructors.Objective:By taking clinical randomized controlled research methods to observe Electro‐acupuncture the Hypochondriac Pain Cause by Cholelithiasis and Preliminary Study of its Efficacy£¬and evaluate the modulating effect of Electro‐acupuncture the Hypochondriac Pain Cause by Cholelithiasis and Preliminary Study of its Efficacy by treatment of Electroacupuncture combined with "Jin Sanzhen". Methods: To select 60 sub‐health patients with physical pain who meet the inclusion criteria from Second Affiliated Hospital of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Medicine, and divide them into treatment group andcontrol group by simple random method .According to exclusion criteria, there are all 60 cases included, of which 30 cases compose treatment group, the rest 30 cases compose the control group. Before the treatment and 1 hour after the treatment, by observing the changes of the two groups indicators of McGill pain question(MPQ) twice, to evaluate the clinical effect. To establish the database and then take statistical analysis with SPSS16.O.To analyze numerical variable with t test, ategorical variable with XZ test and correction Xz test (or the exactprobability method)£¬ranked data with rank sum test and to take Bilateral test. Results: 1. The general information including gender, age, course of disease,WHOQOL‐BRIEF scores, MPQ indicators of the two groups, there is no (P>0.05).the baselines of the two groups are basically the same before treatment. 2. To compare the indicators of McGill pain question (SF‐MPQ) before and after the treatment of the two groups, there is significant difference (P<0. 05) between the indicators of PRI, VAS, PPI before and after treatment of the treatment group. It shows that there has been significant PRI,VAS,PPI after taking the Electro‐acupuncture. 3. To compare the indicators of McGill pain question (SF‐MPQ) after the treatment of the two groups, there is significant difference (P<0.05) between the indicators of PRI, AVS, PPI. It shows there has been significant PRI, VAS, PPI between two groups. 4. To compare the indicators of McGill pain question (SF‐MPQ) AT after the treatment of the two groups, there is significant difference(P<0. 05) between two groups. And the AT summary of the treatment group was bigger than the .AT summary of the control group. It shows that the improvement of PRI, VAS, PPI of the treatment group surpass that of the control group. Conclusion: Electro‐acupuncture is an effective method to the treatment of Hypochondriac Pain Cause by Cholelithiasis,United the indicators of McGill pain question (SF‐MPQ) after the treatment of the two groups, and the AT summary, we can make the Conclusion:Electro‐acupuncture combined with "Jin Sanzhen" is better than Simple electroacupuncture on treatment of the Hypochondriac Pain Cause by Cholelithiasis and Preliminary Study of its Efficacy. It can improve the clinical integrated effect and to add one more effective therapy to Modulate the sub health with physical pain.
