AB  -  Objective: To search for a economical, safe and effective treatment method for early postoperative inflammatory small bowl obstruction(EPISBO). Methods: Total 60 patients observed with EPISBO were randomized into two groups. Group A was western medicine alone treatment group (30 cases). Group B was the combined treatment group of modified Chengqi decoction retention enema joining electro‐acupuncture besides western medicine (30 cases). Results: The total efficiency of group A was 86.7%, group B was 93.3%, there were significant differences between the two groups (P<0.05). The average recovery time of bowel sound was (8.6+2.5) days in group A and (6.5+3.1) days in group B, the mean anus exhaust time was (9.4+3.5) days in group A and (7.1+3.2) days in group B, group B was more effective than group A. The level of serum WBC CRP decreased more after treatment in group B than in group A, the differences was statically significant (P<0.05); and the level of serum ALB increased more after treatment in group B than in group 0.05. In two groups the levels of serum TNF‐¦Á, IL‐6 were dropped after treatment, and group B was dropped significantly than group A(P <0.05). The level of serum IL‐10 was increased after treatment in two groups, and group B was increased significantly than group A(P<0.05). Conclusion: The combined application of modified Chengqi decoction retention enema joining electro‐acupuncture in treatment of EPISBO embodies the characteristics of traditional Chinese and western medicine. It can shorten the course of treatment, inhibit the release of pro inflammatory cytokines and promote anti inflammatory cytokines secretion. It can relieve edema of intestinal wall reduce the loss of plasma protein. The recovery of gastrointestinal function is promoted, the effectiveness of treatment is improved, and the treatment effect is also satisfied.
