AB  -  Objective: To compare the clinical efficacy of electroacupuncture at Bliao point combined with oral mifepristone tablets and oral mifepristone tablets alone in the treatment of residual intrauterine tissue after incomplete abortion and hysterectomy and its effect on uterine cavity volume involution. Methods: Fifty‐eight patients with incomplete abortion after hysterectomy were randomly divided into electroacupuncture group and western medicine group, 29 cases in each group. The western medicine group was treated with oral mifepristone tablets, 2 tablets each time, once a day; the electro‐acupuncture group received electro‐acupuncture at Bliao points (Shangliao, Ciliao, Zhongliao, and Xialiao) on the basis of the western medicine group, and the density wave , once a day, 50min each time, the two groups were treated for 3d as a course of treatment, a 1d rest after a course of treatment, a total of 2 courses of treatment. The residual area of ​​intrauterine tissue and the positive rate of color Doppler flow imaging (CDFI) blood flow signals in the two groups of patients before and after treatment were recorded; the days of vaginal bleeding and the rate of secondary surgery were recorded in the two groups of patients after treatment, and the two groups were measured by three‐dimensional ultrasound reconstruction. The endometrial volume of the patients after menstrual rehydration was measured, and the clinical efficacy was evaluated. Results: After treatment, the residual area of ​​intrauterine tissue in the two groups decreased compared with before treatment, and the positive rate of CDFI blood flow signal was lower than that before treatment (P<0.05). The positive rate of CDFI blood flow signal was lower than that of western medicine group (P<0.05). After treatment, the days of vaginal bleeding in the electroacupuncture group were shorter than those in the western medicine group, the second surgery rate was lower than that in the western medicine group (P<0.05), and the endometrial volume after menstruation was greater than that in the western medicine group (P<0.05). The total effective rate in the electroacupuncture group was 55.2% (16/29), which was higher than that in the western medicine group, which was 37.9% (11/29, P<0.05). Conclusion: Electro‐acupuncture at Bliao point combined with oral administration of mifepristone tablets can effectively promote uterine contraction, soften and expel residual tissue in the uterus in patients with incomplete abortion after hysterectomy, which is beneficial to the involution of uterine cavity volume, and its curative effect is better than that of oral mifepristone alone. Keto tablets.
