AB  -  INTERVENTION: Treatment Group: Electroacupuncture Group:Operation: the patient takes the prone position, the whole body relaxes, the routine disinfection. Acupuncture at ciliao (BL 30) and Zhongliao (BL 30) was applied with 0.40 * 125 mm filiform needle at an angle of 60 ° downward into the posterior sacral foramen of s 2 and S 3 at an angle of 110‐120 mm Shenshu and Sanyinjiao were punctured with 0.30 mm * 40 mm filiform needle at 25 35 mm, and all acupoints were punctured on the basis of Qi, then SDZ‐V electro‐acupuncture apparatus with paired electrodes was applied to the bilateral acupoints of ciliao, ciliao, Huiyang and Sanyinjiao, respectively. The continuous wave, with a frequency of 4 Hz, was applied to increase the current intensity slowly for 30 min. Course of treatment: the total treatment time was 4 weeks, 5 times a week in the first 2 weeks and 3 times a week in the last 2 weeks, totaling 16 times.;Control group: sham electroacupuncture group:In SDZ‐V electro‐acupuncture apparatus, two pairs of electrodes were connected to bilateral Zhongliao, ciliao, Huiyang and Sanyinjiao points respectively, and all points were punctured 2‐3mm, do not mention the twist can not air, needle upright and can withstand the electrode for degrees, keep the needle for 30 minutes.; CONDITION: Overactive Bladder PRIMARY OUTCOME: Overactive Bladder Symptom Scale, OABSS; SECONDARY OUTCOME: patient perception bladder condition score PPBC;Overactive Bladder Questionnaire OAB‐q;Self‐Rating Anxiety Scale,SAS;Self‐Rating Depression Scale,SDS;Overactive Bladder Symptom Scale, OABSS; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) the OABSS score =3 and the symptom score =2 were in accordance with the diagnostic criteria of refractory OAB; (2) aged 18‐60 years; (3) be able to communicate well with researchers and willing to comply with the requirements of the whole experiment; (4) volunteer to participate in the experiment and sign the informed consent form; (5) not received any other treatment in the 