AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Carticosteroid injection with electroacupuncture: 1 ml Triamcinolone Acetonide (10 mg/ml) (Kenacort‐ A 10) with 1 ml Lignocaine (1%) [Corticosteroid injection] will be administered into the most palpably tender point(s) in the region of the wrist. Electroacupuncture therapy is a multidisciplinary approach used in orthopaedics, physiotherapy, sports medicine, urology and veterinary medicine. Its main assets are fast pain relief and mobility restoration. Together with being a non‐surgical therapy with no need for painkillers makes it an ideal therapy to speed up recovery and cure various indications causing acute or chronic pain. The treatment was given 4 days in a week for 4v weeks. Control Intervention1: Caricosteroid injection with placebo Electroacupuncture: 1 ml Triamcinolone Acetonide (10 mg/ml) (Kenacort‐ A 10) with 1 ml Lignocaine (1%) [Corticosteroid injection] will be administered into the most palpably tender point(s) in the region of the wrist. Placebo electro acupuncture therapy The treatment was given 4 days in a week for 4v weeks. CONDITION: Health Condition 1: M95‐M95‐ Other disorders of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissue PRIMARY OUTCOME: 1. Pain intensity â?? VAS ; 2. Ultra sound analysis ‐ ; 3. Functional disability ‐ Boston Questionnaire ; 4. Hand grip â?? Hand dynamometer ; Timepoint: Baseline, after 4 weeks, 8 weeks and 6 months ; SECONDARY OUTCOME: 1. Kinesiophobia â?? Tampa scale ; 2. Depression â?? Hospital anxiety and depression scale ; 3. Quality of life â?? Euro Qol EQ‐5D ; Timepoint: Baseline, after 4 weeks, 8 weeks and 6 months ; INCLUSION CRITERIA: Diagnosis of the mild or moderate stage of CTS (according to criteria by Whitney and McDonnell) by an orthopedist or neurologist, symptom duration for more than three months, and general good health.
