AB  -  INTERVENTION: Trial Group:Electro‐acupuncture therapy: Four pairs of acupoints (Taixi, Shuiquan, Hegu, Sanyinjiao) were selected, with anatomical positioning based on the national standard 'Names and Locations of Acupoints' (GB/T 12346‐2006). 0.30 mm × 40 mm disposable sterile acupuncture needles were used, administered by licensed Chinese medical practitioners. After routine disinfection and adhesive pad fixation, the needles were inserted 30–50 mm deep into each acupoint: Shuiquan, Taixi, Hegu, and Sanyinjiao. Subsequent manipulation included small rotation, lifting, and thrusting to achieve deqi. The SDZ‐III electroacupuncture device (Suzhou Medical Supplies Factory Co., Ltd.) was connected, with paired acupoints on the same side of the body, avoiding crossing the heart. A sparse‐dense wave pattern was applied at a frequency of 2 Hz/15 Hz, with current intensity adjusted to the maximum tolerable level (slight skin twitching without intolerable pain), with needles retained for 20 minutes.;Sham Group:Sham acupuncture: After routine disinfection of the local skin at four acupoints, adhesive pads were placed on the sites. A specially designed blunt‐tipped 1‐cun needle was inserted through the pad to the skin surface without breaking the skin. Each acupoint underwent three manipulations of lifting and thrusting and twirling. The electroacupuncture device was connected but not activated. Needles were retained for 20 minutes.; CONDITION: Catheter‐related bladder discomfort PRIMARY OUTCOME: Severity of CRBD at T1 (5 minutes post‐intervention); SECONDARY OUTCOME: Visual Analog Scale (VAS) for urethral and surgical site pain at T1, T2, and T3;Richmond Agitation‐Sedation Scale (RASS);Hemodynamic parameters including non‐invasive blood pressure (NIBP), pulse oximetry (SpO2), and heart rate (HR) at T0, T1, T2, and T3;Use of rescue medication (oxycodone);Incidence of adverse events related to electroacupuncture;Use of other medications during the study period; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Undergoing elective non‐cardiac surgery under general anesthesia 2. Aged 18 to 60 years 3. Body Mass Inde X(BMI) between 18 and 30 4. Preoperative ASA Physical Status Classification I to III 5. Patients who complain of catheter‐related bladder discomfort after tracheal extubation in the PACU 6. Fully understand the trial protocol and objectives and have signed the informed consent form
