AB  -  INTERVENTION: Experimental Group 1:Main Acupuncture Points: Zusanli, Shangjiuxu Electroacupuncture: continuous wave (2HZ), current 0‐40mA (can be accurate to 0.1mA) range of independent adjustment, as tolerated by the patient. Leave the needle in place for 20 mins.;Experimental Group 2:Main Acupuncture Points: Zusanli, Shangjiuxu Electroacupuncture: continuous wave (100HZ), current 0‐40mA (can be accurate to 0.1mA) range of independent adjustment, as tolerated by the patient. Leave the needle in place for 20 mins.;Sham Acupuncture Control Group:Acupuncture points: 3 non‐meridian and non‐acupuncture points were selected, and all needling points were not at meridians and acupoints. Operation: Disposable sterile foam pads were attached to the non‐acupuncture points, and disposable sterile flat‐tipped acupuncture needles were inserted into the foam pads, gently touching but not piercing the skin, without qi, and the positive and negative poles of the electro‐acupuncture needles were connected to the non‐acupuncture points at 1/2 of the non‐acupuncture points, without electricity, and the needles were left in place for 20 min. After the needles were activated, the foam pads were gently removed from the subject's body surface.;Healthy Control Group:Only one MRI scan was received during the trial and no treatment was required.; CONDITION: Irritable bowel syndrome PRIMARY OUTCOME: IBS Symptom Severity; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Effective Response Rate;Irritable Bowel Syndrome Overall Symptoms;Patient Depression Score;Irritable Bowel Syndrome Quality of Life Status;Bowel Movement Frequency;Abdominal Pain Symptoms;Adequate remission of IBS symptoms;Abdominal Bloating Symptoms; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Age between 18 and 75 years old (inclusive), gender not limited; 2. Meet the diagnostic criteria for subtypes of Rome IV diarrhea‐predominant irritable bowel syndrome; 3. In the past two weeks, the daily defecation diary report shows at least 4 days of Bristol stool type 6 or 7 and less than 4 days of Bristol stool type 1 or 2. The average daily abdominal pain score in the past week was >=3 points. 4. No acupuncture treatment has been received in the past si Xmonths; 5. No antidepressants or drugs that treat the symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome have been taken within two weeks before treatment, including traditional Chinese medicine or Chinese patent medicine, antidiarrheal drugs, antispasmodics, intestinal antibiotics, probiotic preparations, etc. Only those who meet all the above requirements can be included.
