AB  -  INTERVENTION: Procedure/Surgery : <Experimental group> 1) treatment tools ‐Among the sterilized stainless steel of 0.5*50mm, 0.5*80mm, 0.75*50mm, and 0.75*80mm sized needles to be used in the study (Dongbang, Korea), the appropriate acupotomy for the treatment site is used according to the judgment of the clinical trial practitioner. ? It was decided not to use acupotomy with a diameter of 1.0mm in accordance with the opinions of practitioners at clinical research institutes that it may cause pain and damage. The 0.75 and 0.5 sizes are choose according to the practitioner's preference. In addition, it is possible to make a choice according to the sensitivity of the patient's pain. And the used needle size should be recorded on the case record form. <Control group> 1) The scope of usual Korean Medicine treatment (1) Acupuncture, moxibustion, cupping therapy, chuna therapy, herbal acupuncture therapy, physio therapy (excluding herbal medicine) are can be performed, except for acupotomy, at the judgment of the practitioner. Acupuncture (including electro‐acupuncture), cupping therapy, and physio therapy (infra red, etc.) are essential, and moxibustion therapy, chuna therapy, and herbal acupuncture therapy can be performed selectively. (Those who want to take herbal medicine can be applied their own expense, just record the details on the case record form) ‐ In the case of the usual Korean Medicine treatment group, various treatment interventions can be applied except for acupotomy in order to implement the treatment method at the real world. CONDITION: Diseases of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissue PRIMARY OUTCOME: Oswestry low back disability questionnaire SECONDARY OUTCOME: Additional prodecure or surgery perform rate Cost‐effectiveness assessment(Direct medical expenses, Direct non‐medical expenses, iMTA Productivity Cost Questionnaire) McGill pain Questionnaire NRS of low back and radiating pain Premature termination rate Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire Safety assessment(Physical examination, Vital sign, PRO‐CTCAE, Adverse events) The 5‐level European Quality of Life 5 Dimension(EQ‐5D‐5L) Treatment responder, non‐responder assessment Use of rescue drug INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1) Adult men and women aged 19‐85 2) Those who have been diagnosed with spondylosis with lumbosacral disc disorder (injury), spinal stenosis, lumbosacral radiculopathy. through radiological examination (MRI or CT) within 6 months prior to participation in the clinical trial (In the case of a patient suspected of lumbosacral radiculopathy but no imaging record at the time of the screening test, MRI or CT scans are performed to check whether it meets the diagnostic criteria) 3) Patients who have symptoms related to lumbosacral radiculopathy, such as radiological pain, muscle weakness, and paresthesia of the lower extremities, or who have been diagnosed with radiculopathy of the lumbosacral spine through a physical examination. 4) Patients with NRS 4 or higher with pain/discomfort due to lumbosacral radiculopathy 5) Patients who read the symptom questionnaire and can understand and answer its meaning 6) Patients who voluntarily consent to the approv
