AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: MERIDIAN BALANCE METHOD ACUPUNCTURE: STEP 1:Detailed questions are asked from the patient about the location, type, aggravating factor and the severity of pain. The patient is made to sit comfortably on a chair or stool. After assessing the exact location of the pain, Sick meridian is identified either UB or GV meridian. Step 2:consists of choosing the balancing meridian according to the pain in area, for example if pain is in UB meridian, it can be balanced by SI, Heart, kidney or Lung meridians. After choosing the treating meridian the points are selected according to the Mirror Imaging or Reverse mirror Imaging replicating back image on the hands or legs. Tender points are selected and needled (mainly SI 3, SI 4, SI 5). With the combination of Tung’s acupuncture using Lingu, Dabai, Zongbai and Xiabai on opposite hand the patient get relief from pain within 10 seconds of needling. The needle was left retained for 20 minutes. This procedure lasted about 25 minutes. Control Intervention1: Electroacupuncture: This group has been treated with the application of acupuncture needles with the help of electric current aka Electroacupuncture(EA).EA group was retained for 20 minutes.It was applied connected to the points BL23, BL27,BL30, BL52 and bilateral GV4.The intensity of stimulation was increased according to comfort of the patient.This procedure lasted about 25 minutes. CONDITION: Health Condition 1: M51‐ Thoracic, thoracolumbar, and lumbosacral intervertebral disc disorders PRIMARY OUTCOME: Visual Analogue Scale (VAS),McGill Pain Questionnaire,Goniometer,OSWESTRY DISABILITY INDEX,PAIN DISABILITY INDEX,Timepoint: 2 time points(baseline and after 20 minutes) SECONDARY OUTCOME: Insomnia Severity IndexTimepoint: 2 time points(baseline and after 20 minutes) INCLUSION CRITERIA: Age 25‐70, Both males and females will be included, Preoperative visual analogue scale (VAS) score =4, Decreased range of motion, Persistent pain more than 6 months, Independently mobile (with or without aids)
