AB  -  INTERVENTION: Medical Device : This study is a single center, prospective, 2‐arm, parallel, assessor‐blind, randomized controlled trial. Participants assigned to the experimental group (acupuncture plus usual care) will receive 12 acupuncture sessions for 3 months in addition to the usual management of postoperative pain. Stainless‐steel disposable acupuncture needles (0.20 X30 mm, 0.25 X30 mm, 0.25 X40 mm or 0.30 X60 mm, Dongbang Inc., Ltd.,Republic of Korea) and electroacupuncture (ES‐160, Ito Co. Ltd., Japan) will be used. Participants assigned to the control group (usual care only) will perform routine management of postoperative pain without receiving acupuncture. The total study duration is 24 weeks, including follow‐up period. CONDITION: Injury, poisoning and certain other consequences of external causes PRIMARY OUTCOME: Adherence proportion to acupuncture treatment Trial completion proportion Trial participation proportion SECONDARY OUTCOME: Adverse events Pain NRS Patient global assessment Pulmonary function test Quality of life Trial dropout proportion Use of medications INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Multiple traumatic rib fractures treated with thoracotomy at the Pusan University Hospital Trauma Center 2. Patients aged 19 to 80 years 3. A period of over 1 month since the surgery was performed 4. Pain intensity numeric rating scale (NRS) score of at least 4 during rest, movement, or coughing over the last week 5. Patients who agree to the research purpose and provided the written informed consent 6. Responses to the study questionnaire can be performed by the participant himself/herself or with the assistance of the participant's protector or researcher.
