AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Meridian balance method acupuncture: Detailed questions are asked of the patient about the location, type, aggravating factor, and severity of pain. The patient is made to sit comfortably on a chair or stool. After assessing the exact location of the pain, the Sick meridian is identified as either ST or SP meridian or both ST and SP. Step 2 consists of choosing the balancing meridian according to the pain in the area, for example, if the pain is in ST meridian, it can be balanced by LI, SP or P meridians, and if the pain is in SP meridian, it is balanced by either LU, SI, ST or TW meridian. After choosing the treating meridian the points are selected according to the Mirror Imaging or Reverse mirror Imaging replicating knee image on the elbow joint. Tender points are selected and needled (mainly LI11, LI10, LI12, OR LU5, and nearby tender points). With the combination of Tung’s acupuncture using Mu Huo (11.10), ZongJian (11.05), SiHuaZhong (77.09), SiHuaXia (77.011) on the opposite hand, and SanJin (DT.07). The needles left retained for 20 minutes and this procedure lasts for about 25 minutes. Control Intervention1: Electroacupuncture: The patient is made to sit comfortably on a chair or stool. This group has been treated with the application of acupuncture needles with the help of electric current aka Electroacupuncture. Needles were kept for 20 minutes. Electrical stimulation was applied connected to the points ST35, EX‐LE4, EX‐LE2, SP10, ST36, GB34, SP9, and BL40. The intensity of stimulation was increased according to the comfort of the patient. This procedure lasts for 25 minutes. CONDITION: Health Condition 1: M17‐ Osteoarthritis of knee PRIMARY OUTCOME: Visual Analogue Scale (VAS), McGill Pain Questionnaire, Goniometer,Pain disability index, WOMAC scaleTimepoint: 2 time points(baseline and after 20 minutes) SECONDARY OUTCOME: Insomnia Severity IndexTimepoint: 2 time points(baseline and after 20 minutes) INCLUSION CRITERIA: Age 25‐70, Both males and females will be included, Preoperative visual analogue scale (VAS) score =4, Decreased range of motion, Persistent pain more than 6 months,Independently mobile (with or without aids)
