AB  -  n this study, we investigated the clinical efficacy and poor prognosis of patients with imb disorders after the operation of hypertensive cerebral hemorrhage, using the reatment of removing blood stasis and Shengxin acupuncture combined with early ehabilitation training using a randomized trial. A total of 100 patients with the ypertensive intracerebral hemorrhage who underwent surgery in our hospital from ay 2019 to May 2021 were selected and divided into control group were treated with arly rehabilitation training, and the intervention group was treated with acupuncture or removing blood stasis and promoting new acupuncture based on the control group. e observed that there was no significant difference in the evaluation of limb function ecovery between the two groups of patients (P>0.05). After the intervention, the odified Ashworth score, FMA score, and B1 index of the two groups were ignificantly different in the ADL scores and the scores of families and friends support ere remarkably improved. The clinical treatment efficiency of the intervention group as 94.00%, significantly higher than that of the control group of 80.00%, and the ifference was statistically significant (P<0.05). The study demonstrated that the ehabilitation training combined with removing blood stasis and Shengxin acupuncture s significantly better than rehabilitation training alone to improve postoperative limb ysfunction, daily life and quality of life and is a clinical treatment for hypertension.
