AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention group:The intervention group will, after entering the operating room on the day of surgery, in addition to undergoing routine monitoring (such as heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen saturation, electrocardiogram, and bispectral index) and establishing an intravenous line, also have a percutaneous electrical nerve stimulation device connected to the Hegu, Neiguan, Houxi, and Zhigou acupoints on both sides after intravenous administration of midazolam. They will then receive 30 minutes of electrical stimulation before the induction of anesthesia begins. After the anesthesia induction is completed, the percutaneous electrical nerve stimulation will continue at an intensity of 30 mA until the end of the surgery.;Control group:In this study, patients in the control group will, after entering the operating room on the day of surgery, undergo routine monitoring (including heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen saturation, electrocardiogram, and bispectral index) and have an intravenous line established. Subsequently, after intravenous administration of midazolam, anesthesia induction will begin, with the process being identical to that of the intervention group. After the anesthesia induction is completed, patients in the control group will not receive percutaneous electrical nerve stimulation, but other nursing measures will be the same as those for the intervention group. Postoperatively, patients in the control group will receive routine postoperative care, including postoperative monitoring and the use of antiemetic drugs if necessary. Researchers will record indicators such as the incidence, duration of postoperative nausea and vomiting, and the use of antiemetic drugs within 24 hours after surgery to assess the postoperative nausea and vomiting situation in the c CONDITION: Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting PRIMARY OUTCOME: Incidence of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting;Duration of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting;Usage of Antiemetic Drugs;Patient Satisfaction; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Time to Relief of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1.Patients with ASA physical status classification of I–II; 2.Patients with no history of anesthesia within the past year; 3.Patients who have not used antiemetic drugs within 1 month before surgery; 4.Patients aged 18–65 years; 5.Patients without severe cardiovascular disease, diabetes, or liver and kidney disease; 6.Patients without psychiatric abnormalities or language communication barriers.
