AB  -  INTERVENTION: Cyclophenol group:Induction was performed by intravenous infusion of cyclophenol (0.3‐0.5mg/kg), remifentanil (TCI1‐3ng/ml), sufentanil (0.2‐0.4 µ g/kg), and cisatracurium (0.2mg/kg) after denitrification and oxygenation. After the muscles relax, insert the tracheal tube smoothly. By administering cyclosporine, remifentanil, inhaling sevoflurane, and maintaining anesthesia. Continuous intravenous infusion of 2 µ g/(kg*min) of cisatracurium or administration as needed based on intraoperative conditions.;Electroacupuncture acupoint group:Starting 10 minutes before surgery, constant and continuous current transcutaneous electrical stimulation (instrument: Beijing Yaoyang Kangda Medical Instrument ‐ transcutaneous nerve electrical stimulation device KD‐2B) was applied at Shenmen point, Tongli point, and Sanyinjiao point. The parameters were set to continuous wave, frequency of 70Hz, pulse width of 30us, current intensity of 6mA, and continued until the end of the surgery. After nitrogen and oxygen removal, induction was performed by intravenous infusion of propofol (TCI1‐3ug/ml), remifentanil (TCI1‐3ng/ml), sufentanil (0.2‐0.4 µ g/kg), and cisatracurium (0.2mg/kg). After the muscles relax, insert the tracheal tube smoothly. Administer propofol, remifentanil, inhaled sevoflurane, and maintain anesthesia. Continuous intravenous infusion of 2 µ g/(kg8min) of cisatracurium or administration as needed based on intraoperative conditions.;Joint group:Starting 10 minutes before surgery, constant continuous current transcutaneous electrical stimulation (instrument: Beijing Yaoyang Kangda Medical Instrument ‐ transcutaneous nerve electrical stimulator KD‐2B) was applied at Shenmen point, Tongli point, and Sanyinjiao point, with parameters set as continuous wave, frequency of 70HZ, pu CONDITION: Sleep disorders PRIMARY OUTCOME: Athens Insomnia Scale Score;Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index Scale;Non invasive cardiac output;Peripheral vascular resistance; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Blood pressure and heart rate; Collect relevant data on the preoperative and postoperative sleep monitoring wristbands on day 1 (including all day sleep duration),The duration of sleep, deep sleep time throughout the day, light sleep time throughout the day, wakefulness time, time of falling asleep last night, time of waking up this morning, and based on body movements during sleep. ; INCLUSION CRITERIA: Age >= 55 years old, ASA II‐III grade, BMI18‐25kg/m^2, Hypertensive patients undergoing urological surgery, including various stones and tumors (excluding functional tumors such as pheochromocytoma and primary aldosteronism), without serious systemic diseases, voluntarily participate in this trial and sign an informed consent form.
