AB  -  INTERVENTION: Acupoint electrical stimulation group (T group):TEAS acupoint physical therapy electrode stimulation group (T group). The acupoints of the subjects were selected according to the standard acupuncture nomenclature of the second edition of the China (GB/12346‐2006), Dazhui (DU14), bilateral Shenmen (HT7) and Neiguan (PC6). In the afternoon of the day before the operation, we visited the patient in the ward, cleaned the skin with alcohol at the acupoint, pasted the pulse heating gel electrode (Camel Medical Instrument TR‐1), and started TEAS for 30 minutes after lying on the back to keep warm for 30 minutes (T0). The acupoint stimulation of experimental group T was given by density wave, with the frequency of 2 Hz/100 Hz, The intensity is 8‐30 mA (taking the maximum intensity value that the patient can tolerate, with a temperature of 38‐40 ?. The wrist strap monitoring records the sleep quality of the night of treatment. On the day of surgery, the patient enters the room and the acupoint treatment method is grouped according to the same preoperative method. All patients use a medical temperature controller (Zhuhai Heima Medical Instrument) to keep warm during surgery, and a constant temperature liquid storage cabinet (FYL‐YS828L, Beijing Fuyilian Electric Appliances) is used to warm and infuse the same temperature liquid and flushing solution (22 ?). The Mindray (T9) anesthesia monitor continuously monitors body temperature and whether shivers occur 30 minutes before treatment (T0), 30 minutes after anesthesia (T0), 60 minutes after surgery (T1), 120 minutes after surgery (T2), 180 minutes after surgery (T3), and after surgery (T4).;Control group (Group C):Group C only applied electrode patches to acupoints but did not receive electrical stimulation, but informed the subje CONDITION: 68.405 Laparoscopic total hysterectomy PRIMARY OUTCOME: Postoperative hypothermia incidence;Postoperative shivering incidence;Preoperative and intraoperative body temperature at different time points; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Mean arterial pressure at different time points before and during operation;Sleep quality;Operative time;Total infusion volume;Amount of peritoneal flushing fluid; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Patients undergoing elective laparoscopic total Hysterectomy; (1) Age range from 36 to 70 years old; (3) The American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) is classified as Grade I‐II; (4) Sign an informed consent form.
