AB  -  INTERVENTION: acupuncture group:Patients in the electroacupuncture (EA) group received electroacupuncture preconditioning 30 minutes before surgery by qualified physicians holding dual licenses in Western medicine and Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) after being transferred to the pre‐anesthetic room. The selected acupoints included Yintang (EX‐HN3), Shenting (GV24), bilateral Taixi (KI3), Shenmen (HT7), Neiguan (PC6), and Hegu (LI4) (Table 1, Figure 1). After the acupoints were disinfected with alcohol swabs, 0.3 mm × 40 mm filiform needles were inserted perpendicularly. The lifting‐thrusting and twirling‐rotating manipulation was applied to the selected acupoints at a depth of approximately 1–2 cun. The needle handles were then connected to an electronic acupuncture therapeutic apparatus with dense‐disperse wave (2/15 Hz) at an intensity of 2 mA, and continuous stimulation was delivered for 30 minutes, with the intensity adjusted to the patient’s tolerance level. Upon completion of the procedure, the output intensity was first reduced to zero before the power was turned off. Subsequently, the electrode clips were removed and the needles were withdrawn.;non‐acupuncture group:Non‐acupuncture group patients underwent direct combined intravenous‐inhalation general anesthesia with endotracheal intubation in the operating room without prior electroacupuncture.; CONDITION: Perioperative elderly patients with mild cognitive impairment PRIMARY OUTCOME: incidence of Postoperative Delirium; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Phosphorylated Tau at Threonine 217;Montreal Cognitive Assessment;Mini‐Mental State Examination;Visual Analogue Scale; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Patients aged 65 years and older; 2. Patients diagnosed with mild cognitive impairment (MCI) preoperatively; 3. American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) physical status Grade I–II; 4. Scheduled for elective lower extremity joint replacement surgery (total knee arthroplasty or total hip arthroplasty).
