AB  -  INTERVENTION: Electroacupuncture Group:Electroacupuncture intervention was performed in the preoperative waiting area on the day of operation. The patient underwent electroacupuncture treatment, and the acupuncture point selection was: Baihui Neiguan (double) Hegu (double) Zusanli (double). After routine disinfection, 0.30mm × 40mm millimeter needle was used to insert needles directly with both hands, flat replenishing and flat draining method was performed, and 1 needle was needled 1 inch outward in Zusanli as an auxiliary needle. Four groups on both sides were treated with denser wave therapy. Orientation: Refer to "Acupuncture and moxibustion", the planning textbook for Chinese medicine colleges and universities in China edited by Shi Xuemin. Then, the electroacupuncture apparatus was connected, Hegu was connected to Neiguan, and Zusanli was connected to auxiliary acupuncture. The density wave type was selected, and the current intensity was tolerated by the patient. The induction lasted for 30 min. After entering the operating room, electroacupuncture induction was continued until the end of the operation, and the other steps were the same as the control group. The needle was removed after the patient woke up under anesthesia. All procedures are performed by the same team of surgeons and anesthesiologists.;Control Group:On the basis of conventional treatment, simulated electroacupuncture was used to perform blank control treatment. Acupuncture needles and acupuncture points were the same as those in electroacupuncture group. Cover the patients acupoint with microporous medical tape, and place the acupuncture needle in the hole of the medical tape (without penetrating the skin).; CONDITION: Intracranial aneurysm PRIMARY OUTCOME: opioid‐related adverse events; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Postoperative analgesic drug consumption;Maximum postoperative pain score at rest and during exercise;Postoperative incidence of nausea and vomiting;Numbers of requiring posterior antiemetic drugs;Induction to intubation time;Changes in vital signs during intubation; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Patients undergoing elective interventional surgery for intracranial aneurysms; (2) Age > 18 years old; (3) ASA grade I‐III.
