AB  -  INTERVENTION: Experimental Group:Prior to anesthesia induction, routine disinfection of the acupoints (Hegu [LI4], Neiguan [PC6], Zusanli [ST36], and Taichong [LR3]) was performed. Disposable sterile acupuncture needles were inserted perpendicularly and rotated to a depth of 1–2 inches until deqi sensation was achieved. The needle handles were then connected to an electroacupuncture device. The stimulatio was applied for 30 minutes;Control group:Prior to anesthesia induction, following routine skin disinfection, disposable sterile acupuncture needles were inserted 2 cm adjacent to the acupoints with subcutaneous penetration of the needle tip, at which point insertion was terminated. The needle handles were then connected to an electroacupuncture device for a 30‐minute stimulation period.; CONDITION: Quality of Recovery After Anesthesia for Nasal Endoscopic Surgery PRIMARY OUTCOME: Quality of Recovery‐15 scale (QoR‐15) at 24 hours postoperatively; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Postoperative Numerical Rating Scale (NRS) Pain Scores at 30min, 2h, and 24h;Anesthetic Drug Consumption During Surgery;Extubation time;Intraoperative Cardiovascular Drug Administration;Postoperative 24‐hour analgesic consumption;Intraoperative opioid consumption;Post‐Anesthesia Care Unit (PACU) Length of Stay; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1: Adult patients (18‐65 years) of either se Xrequiring general anesthesia for functional endoscopic sinus surgery. 2: ASA I‐II patients with BMI <30 kg/m² 3: No history of relevant drug allergies 4: Cognitively capable of completing NRS and QoR assessments and willing to participate with signed informed consent
