AB  -  INTERVENTION: electroacupuncture :Before the whole brain angiography (DSA) examination, the following acupuncture points are: bilateral Hegu (LI4), Neiguan (PC6), Zusanli (ST36), Shenmen (HT7), Yintang (EX‐HN3). Use disposable sterile stainless steel needles for treatment. After inserting the needle, the acupuncturist does the needle until the patient reaches a sense of breath. Two pairs of electrodes of the electroacupuncture instrument are connected to the acupuncture needles of LI4 and ST36 on both sides, providing continuous waves with low‐frequency (2 Hz) and 2 mA current for 20‐30 minutes of continuous treatment. ;Non‐acupoint shallow acupuncture group(SA):The acupuncturist used non‐acupoints for superficial acupuncture as a control. Use the same needle to insert the surface depth as the EA group. The needle is connected to the electrode for 30 minutes, but does not provide current.; CONDITION: Cerebrovascular disease PRIMARY OUTCOME: Pain visual analogue scale; visual analogue scale of nausea and vomiting; visual analogue scale of resistance and restlessness;visual analogue scale of emotional state; SECONDARY OUTCOME: State‐Trait Anxiety Inventory;Home Against Medical Advice;Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Inde X(PSQI); INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) men or women aged 18‐80; (2) patients undergoing general cerebral angiography or intravascular treatment under general local anesthesia or intubation; (3) patients who fully understand the scale and can complete the evaluation; (4) patients who voluntarily participate and provide informed consent.
