AB  -  INTERVENTION: Procedure/Surgery : Prospective randomized controlled trial with three‐arm, parallel‐group. 1. Intervention 1 = electroacupuncture Materials: Stainless‐steel needle and PG‐306 electroacupuncture device Methods: At least two hours after operation, electroacupuncture for 30 minutes, twice a day (a.m. &amp; p.m.). Maximum 6 times of acupuncture during hospitalization. Acupuncture site (location): LI4(Hapgok, Hegu), PC6(Naegwan, Neiguan), KI6(Johae, Zhaohai), and LR3(Taechung, Taichong). 2. Intervention 2 = sham acupuncture Materials: Park Sham Device (PSD) Methods &amp; acupuncture location: same as electroacupuncture group 3. Control group = No postoperative acupuncture 4. Blinding for electroacupuncture vs. sham acupuncture 1) Electroacupuncture : Acupuncture with stainless‐steel needle (0.25X40mm, DONGBANG Acupuncture Inc., Korea) and electrostimulation with PG‐306 electroacupuncture device (Tokyo, Japan). 2) Sham acupuncture: Acupuncture with Park Sham Device (PSD). PSD is composed of guide tube and Park tube through which needle is inserted. Sham needle has a blunt end which cannot penetrate skin. However, needle is inserted into the tube and it appears to be shortened so it looks like penetrating skin. 3) Real electroacupuncture set and sham acupuncture set (PSD) are identical in shape. Patients are unable to distinguish between real electroacupuncture and sham acupuncture because they have same shape and same sound (fake electrostimulation sound). 5. Blinding for allocation: True electroacupuncture vs. sham acupuncture : blinded Intervention group (true &amp; sham acupuncture) vs. control group : open CONDITION: Diseases of the digestive system PRIMARY OUTCOME: Time of first passing flatus after operation SECONDARY OUTCOME: Bowel sound per minute Postoperative analgesics Postoperative complications Postoperative hospital stay Postoperative nausea and/or vomiting Postoperative pain score Postoperative quality of life questionnaire Protocol failure rate Readmission rate due to postoperative complications Time to mobilization(self walking) and self support to preoperative level Time to tolerable water drinking and solid diet after operation Total cost during hospital stay after operation INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Patients diagnosed as appendicitis 2. Female or male patients over 20 years old 3. Patients undergoing laparoscopic appendectomy
