AB  -  INTERVENTION: Electroacupuncture Group:Point Selection: Based on the theory of "simultaneous treatment of the spleen and stomach" and meridian theory, the following bilateral acupoints are selected. Zusanli (ST36): Regulates gastrointestinal motility and exerts anti‐inflammatory effects. Shangjuxu (ST37): Lower He‐Sea point of the Large Intestine meridian, relieves intestinal stagnation and clears fu‐organ obstruction. Xiajuxu (ST39): Lower He‐Sea point of the Small Intestine meridian, regulates and tonifies the spleen and stomach. Neiguan (PC6): Calms the heart and tranquilizes the mind, relieves nausea and vomiting (for PONV). Procedure: Disposable sterile acupuncture needles (Jiajian Medical, 0.25×40mm) are used. Needles are inserted perpendicularly, with lifting, thrusting and twirling manipulations to achieve "De Qi" sensation (soreness, numbness, distension and heaviness). Electrical Stimulation Parameters: Connected to an electroacupuncture apparatus (Hwato SDZ‐III), with dense‐disperse wave (2/100Hz). The intensity is adjusted to the patient's tolerance with slight muscle twitching. Timing and Frequency of Treatment: Starting on the first postoperative day, once daily for 30 minutes each session, continuously for 4 days or until discharge.;Sham electroacupuncture group:Acupoint Selection: Non‐meridian and non‐acupoint points are selected. The location is set 1.5–2.0 cm lateral to the true acupoints, avoiding any known meridian lines. Needling Procedure: Streitberger placebo needles are used (blunt‐tipped, with the needle shaft retracting into the handle upon skin contact, creating the illusion of insertion without causing trauma to the skin surface). Electrical Stimulation: The same electroacupuncture device is connected, with wires attached to the needle handles. No electri CONDITION: Obesity PRIMARY OUTCOME: Time to first flatus after surgery; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Postoperative first bowel movement time;Tolerance time for liquid diet;Usage of Antiemetic Drugs;intake, feeling nauseated, emesis, physical exam, and duration of symptoms (I‐FEED) score;Interleukin‐6;C‐reactive protein;Postoperative hospital stay duration; INCLUSION CRITERIA: Age 18‐80 years old. Meets the indications for bariatric surgery (refer to Chinese guidelines: BMI =32.5 kg/m²; or BMI =27.5 kg/m² with metabolic syndrome), planned for elective laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy/laparoscopic gastric bypass. Normal gastrointestinal function preoperatively, with no history of chronic constipation or diarrhea. Voluntarily signed the informed consent form.
