TI  -  The application of laparoscopy on adhesive intestinal obstruction combined with electroacupuncture
JA  -  Guangdong medical journal [guang dong yi xue]
PY  -  2006
VL  -  27
IS  -  3
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  351‐352
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objectives:To compare the effect of laparoscopy combined with electroacupuncture in treatment of adhesive intestinal obstruction with pure laparoscopy.Methods: 60 cases of adhesive intestinal obstruction(accordance with the inclusion criteria) were divided randomly into laparoscopy release adhesion operation combined with electroacupuncture group (observation group) and pure laparoscopy group(control group), every group had 30 cases. Compared the operation time, intraoperative hemorrhage,hospital time, intestine function recovery time, the number of samples of postoperative analgesia and the rate of postoperative complications, follow up 12 months Results: the operation time of observation group was (57.38¡À8.57)min, and that in control group was (52.92¡À6.95)min, the difference is significant (P<0.05), the intraoperative hemorrhage of observation group was (35.18¡À6.53)min, and that in control group was (37.86¡À7.98)min, the difference is not significant (P>0.05), the hospital time of observation group was (3.41¡À1.37)d, and that in control group was (4.26¡À1.68)d, the difference is significant (P<0.05), the intestine function recovery time of observation group was (12.35¡À7.31)h, and that in control group was (20.02¡À8.42)h, the difference is significant (P<0.01); the number of samples of postoperative analgesia in observation group was one cases, and that in control group was 6 cases, the difference is significant (P<0.05), there were no intestinal leakage, incision infection and incisional hernia in two groups. In 6 months follow‐up the rate of abdominal pain in two groups had not significant difference(P>0.05) , After 12 months follow‐up the rate of abdominal pain in two groups had significant difference(P<0.05). Conclusions: The method of laparoscopy combined with electroacupuncture in treatment of adhesive intestinal obstruction have shorter operation time, faster recovery and less abdominal pain.
