AB  -  INTERVENTION: acupuncture group:The foot Sanli, the upper Juxu and Yanglingquan were operated with intelligent electroacupuncture to unify the amount of needling, and the continuous wave was used, with a pulse frequency of 2 Hz and a current of 1‐2 mA, to the extent tolerated by the patient; the Neiguan point was stabbed and then operated with a flat tonic and flat diarrhoeal operation for 30 s to obtain a sense of gaining qi. Treatment: 1 time/day, leave the needle for 30 min, treatment for 4 days, once a day.;control group:The acupoints were the same as the experimental group acupuncture group points, with the true point 1 inch (the same body inch) beside the non‐meridian non‐acupuncture point. After the needling operation, the patient did not get qi or needle sensation, and no needling manoeuvre was applied. Class Neiguan acupoints shallow prick 0.2‐0.3 inch, so that the needle hanging in the skin, not any manipulation. The remaining points were operated with intelligent electroacupuncture, with electrodes connected to the bilateral class points in the same manner as the needling group, but without current access.; CONDITION: Repair of gastrointestinal function after laparoscopic pancreaticoduodenectomy PRIMARY OUTCOME: Time of first postoperative defecation; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Time to first postoperative bowel movement;Bowel sound recovery time;Tolerating a semi‐liquid diet for the first time;First time to tolerate a solid diet for the first time;Time to first postoperative walk;Number of episodes of postoperative nausea and vomiting;Length of hospitalisation;Gastroparesis Basic Symptom Inde X(GCSI) score; INCLUSION CRITERIA: Those who were diagnosed and determined to undergo laparoscopic pancreaticoduodenectomy; those who had not undergone abdominal surgery within si Xmonths prior to the operation; those who were >18 years of age, both male and female; and those whose patients and family members were aware of the details of the study, who voluntarily signed an informed consent form and cooperated in the completion of the study.
