AB  -  Objective: To discuss the curative effects of electroacupuncture on Zusanli (ST 36) for the treatment of early postoperative inflammatory intestinal obstruction (EPIIO). Methods: 28 cases of EPIIO patients were divided randomly into the electroacupuncture group and control group. 2 groups received same basic treatment, and the electroacupuncture group received electroacupuncture on Zusanli (ST 36). Results: The average of exhaust and defecation time was 2.5d in the treatment group, that of the control group was 10.5d. The differences between two groups were statistically significant (P<0.05). Conclusion: Treatment of electroacupuncture on Zusanli (ST 36) may shorten the exhaust and defecation time, and the curative effect of EPIIO after operation is fine
