TY  -  JOUR
AN  -  CN-02523231
AU  -  吴美荣,
TI  -  Observation on the effect of electroacupuncture plus auricular point sticking on promoting uterine recovery after painless abortion
JA  -  中国妇幼健康研究
PY  -  2017
IS  -  S3
CC  -  Fertility Regulation
SP  -  470
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objective: To evaluate the nursing value of electroacupuncture plus auricular point sticking in promoting uterine recovery after painless induced abortion. Methods: 220 patients with painless artificial abortion were randomly divided into experimental group and control group. The experimental group received electroacupuncture and moxibustion at Guanyuan and Uterine acupoints for 15 minutes, and then massaged endocrine and uterine acupoints with both ears for five days. Intramuscular injection of oxytocin was used to observe the postoperative recovery of the uterus. Results: The bloody lochia time and the CRP value 7 days after operation in the experimental group were lower than those in the control group, and the difference was statistically significant (P <0.01). The number of cases with effusion in the uterine cavity of B‐ultrasound in the experimental group was less than that in the control group, but the difference was not statistically significant (P=0.052). Conclusion: Conclusion: Electroacupuncture plus auricular point sticking can effectively promote the recovery of the uterus after painless abortion. It is easy to learn and worthy of popularization and application in clinical nursing.
UR  -  https://www.cochranelibrary.com/central/doi/10.1002/central/CN-02523231/full
