AB  -  INTERVENTION: Medical Device, Procedure/Surgery : 1. Intervention Name: Electroacupuncture (EA) treatment (1 session per visit, total of 2 sessions, bilateral Zusanli‐Yinlingquan acupoints, continuous wave, 15‐minute stimulation, with the current intensity at the minimum level felt by the participant) 2. Medical Devices Used in the Intervention: Sterilized needles with a size of 0.20mm * 30mm and an electroacupuncture stimulator 3. Differences Between Intervention Groups: Difference in the order of frequency selection 3‐1. Intervention Group 1: 2Hz electroacupuncture treatment at Visit 1 ? 100Hz electroacupuncture treatment at Visit 2 3‐2. Intervention Group 2: 100Hz electroacupuncture treatment at Visit 1 ? 2Hz electroacupuncture treatment at Visit 2 4. Washout Period Between Visits: 1 week CONDITION: Diseases of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissue PRIMARY OUTCOME: Postoperative pain intensity questionnaire SECONDARY OUTCOME: Activity data collected from the smart band Heart rate variability (HRV) parameters collected from the heart rate variability measurement device. Pain questionnaire for the past 24 hours Postoperative pain intensity and pain characteristics questionnaire Pulse diagnostic parameters collected from the pulse measurement device. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Participants who meet all of the following inclusion criteria will be selected: 1) Male or female aged 19 to 80 years. 2) Individuals with post‐surgical pain due to musculoskeletal disorders, with a Numerical Rating Scale (NRS) score of 4 or higher (Disease codes: S72090, S7221.000.00, S72120.000.00, S7230.000.0, S82120, M166.000.01, M8785.000.09, M8785, M1999, M1999.000.02, M171.000.03). 3) Individuals who understand the purpose of this clinical trial and the necessary procedures, are able to respond to the pain questionnaire, and voluntarily sign the informed consent form.
