TI  -  Treatment by electroacupuncture at the lower he-sea points for 40 Cases of early postoperative inflammatory small bowel obstruction
JA  -  Conference proceeding of dissertation collection at the acupuncture society of zhejiang province annual meeting and academic seminar in 2013 [zhe jiang sheng zhen jiu xue hui 2013 xue shu nian hui]
PY  -  2013
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  47‐50
M3  -  Conference Proceeding
AB  -  Objective: To evaluate the effect of treat patients with early postoperative inflammatory small bowel obstruction (EPISBO) by electroacupuncture at the lower he‐sea points. Methods: 80 patients with EPISBO were divided into the combination therapy group (40 cases) and Western medicine treatment group (40 cases). The results of the two groups were compared. Results: In the therapy group, there were 36 cases cured (90.0%). There were 27 cases cured (67.5%) in the Western treatment group with statistically significant differences between the two groups (P<0.05). Conclusion: The effect of using electroacupuncture at the lower he‐sea points to treat EPISBO is definite.
