TI  -  Therapeutic efficacy of modified Dachengqi decoction combined with electroacupuncture in treatment of early postoperative inflammatory ileus: a report of 30 cases
JA  -  Hunan journal of traditional chinese medicine [hu nan zhong yi za zhi]
PY  -  2013
VL  -  29
IS  -  4
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  16‐18
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objective: To observe the therapeutic efficacy of modified Dachengqi decoction combined with electroacupuncture in the treatment of early postoperative inflammatory ileus ( EPII). Methods: Ninety EPII patients were randomly divided into first control group, second control group, and treatment group. The first control group received modified Dachengqi decoction, the second control group received acupuncture, and the treatment group received modified Dachengqi decoction combined with electroacupuncture. The treatment outcomes of the three groups were observed. Results: The total effective rates were 96. 67% in the first control group, 96. 67% in the second control group, and 100% in the treatment group, without significant differences among the three groups ( P<0. 05). However, the treatment group had significantly shorter mean time to recovery of bowel sound, mean time to recovery of passage of gas by anus, and time to disappearance of nausea and vomiting than the first and second control groups. Conclusion: Modified Dachengqi decoction combined with electroacupuncture has good therapeutic efficacy in the treatment of EPII.
