JA  -  Chinese community doctors [zhong guo she qu yi shi]
PY  -  2011
VL  -  13
IS  -  4
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  113
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objective: To research the synergistic effects of Nianlian Huanjie Tang combined with electroacupuncture on early postoperative inflammatory small bowel obstruction(EPISBO). Method: 44 patients with EPISBO were randomly divided into control group(21 people) and traditional Chinese medicine combined with electroacupuncture group(23 people). The former took routine treatments and the latter took comprehensive treatment of self‐prepared Nianlian Huanjie Tang combined with electroacupuncture beside toutine treatments. The relief time of clinical symptoms(abdominal pain, abdominal distension, nausea and vomiting ), the anal exsufflation time and the length of stay have been compared and analyzed. Result: Patients in two groups were both cured. The relief time of clinical symptoms, the anal exsufflation time and the length of stay of traditional Chinese medicine combined with electroacupuncture group were less than their counterparts in the control group. There is a statistically significant difference(P<0.05). Conclusion: There are obvious synergistic effects of Nianlian Huanjie Tang combined with electroacupuncture on early postoperative inflammatory small bowel obstruction.
