JA  -  Journal of sichuan of traditional chines medicine [si chuan zhong yi]
PY  -  2011
VL  -  29
IS  -  8
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  117‐118
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objective: To observe the clinical effect of “Tongfu Jiangqi” acupuncture prescriptions for recovering the gastrointestinal function after cholelithotomy. Methods: 60 after‐cholelithotomy patients determined with stratified sampling method of statistics were randomly divided into two groups, each group had 30 patients. Patients of control group were given postoperative routine treatment. The treatment group was given postoperative routine treatment combined with “Tongfu Jiangqi” acupuncture prescriptions. “Tongfu Jiangqi” acupuncture prescriptions used those points including Tianshu, Yanglingquan, Zusanli,Shangjuxu. After the acupuncture till arrival of qi, an electronic acupuncture was performed with dilatational wave. The course of both two groups was two days. Results: The gastrointestinal recovery time was shorter in treatment group comparing with control group, the difference had statistical significance (p<0.05). Conclusion: “Tongfu Jiangqi” acupuncture prescriptions can promote the recovery of gastrointestinal function after cholelithotomy.
