TI  -  Observations on electroacupuncture plus ginger-separated moxibustion for treatment of cervical carcinoma radical postoperative uroschesis
JA  -  Shanghai journal of acupuncture and moxibustion [shang hai zhen jiu za zhi]
PY  -  2009
VL  -  28
IS  -  4
CC  -  Complementary Medicine
SP  -  195‐196
M3  -  Journal article
AB  -  Objective: To investigate the efficacy of electroacupuncture plus ginger‐separated moxibustion in treating cervical carcinoma radical postoperative uroschesis. Methods: Forty‐six patients with cervical carcinoma radical postoperative uroschesis were randomly allocated to the treatment and control groups, 23 cases each. The treatment group received electroacupuncture plus ginger‐separated moxibustion and the control group, intramuscular injection of neostigmine 1 mg plus bladder training. Both were treated once daily, 5 days as a course. The therapeutic effects were evaluated in the two groups after one course of treatment. Results: The efficacy rate was 100.0% in the treatment group and 73.9% in the control group; there was a statistically significant difference between the two groups (P<0.05). Conclusion: Electroacupuncture plus ginger‐separated moxibustion is a better way to treat cervical carcinoma radical postoperative uroschesis.
