AB  -  INTERVENTION: Others(pharmacopuncture therapy, acupuncture, electroacupuncture, cupping, infrared irradiation) : 1. pharmacopuncture therapy ‐ Specific pharmacopuncture intervention will be chosen by a clinical expert of Korean medicine according to the lesion on imaging, radiating pain in low extremity, pain complaint area, tenderness and will be recorded on Case Report Form(CRF). ‐ Treatment areas : lumbar Hyeopcheok points, major acupuncture points in the lumbar region and Ashi point ‐ pharmacopuncture selection : Specific pharmacopuncture intervention will be chosen by a clinical expert of Korean medicine and every specific information about intervention including the chosen pharmacopuncture type and dosage(ml) will be recorded on Case Report Form(CRF). 2. Conventional Korean medicine treatment 1) Cupping : before acupuncture treatment, it is performed on the back and pelvis for 5 minutes 2) Acupuncture + Electroacupuncture + Infrared irradiation ? Acupuncture points ‐ Compulsory main acupuncture points : EX‐B2, L1‐5 corresponding level of lumbar spinal stenosis. ‐ Individualized auxiliary acupuncture points Lumbar/buttock : Yaoyangguan(GV3), Sinsu(BL23), Daejangsu(BL25), Hwangmun(BL51), Jisil(BL52), Charyo(BL32), Jilbyeon(BL54), Hwando(GB30) and Ashi point Lower extremity : Wijung(BL40), Seungsan(BL57), Wiyang(BL39), Gollyun(BL60), Eumneungcheon(SP9), Yangneungcheon(GB34), Hyeonjong(GB39) and Ashi point ? Details of needling : Considering patient's physique, fear of invasive treatment, and postoperative pain, the kinds of the acupuncture needles and the depth of invasion will be determined along with the stimulation to bring out De qi. ? Electroacupuncture : Electroacupuncture stimulation is applied to the acupuncture needles inserted in the compulsory main acupuncture point CONDITION: Diseases of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissue PRIMARY OUTCOME: Visual analog scale(VAS) SECONDARY OUTCOME: Clinically important difference (CID) EuroQol‐5D‐5L index(EQ‐5D‐5L) Maximum walking distance Modified‐Modified Schober Test(MMST) Patient Global Impression of change (PGIC) Safety assessment(Adverse effect) Zurich claudication questionaire (ZCQ) INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Diagnosed with lumbar spinal stenosis by CT or MRI. ‐ If there is no existing image data or if re‐examination is necessary, L‐spine CT scan will be performed 2. Pain or discomfort in the lower extremities/buttocks = VAS 40mm 3. Those who have clinical features of spinal stenosis, such as neurogenic claudication or changes in symptoms due to position 4. Those who are finally diagnosed with lumbar spinal stenosis as a result of a comprehensive physical examination, medical history examination, and imaging examination 5. Those who voluntarily decide to participate after hearing the explanation of the research purpose and process and consent in writing
