AB  -  INTERVENTION: Control group:The control group received a sham acupuncture treatment using specially designed round‐tip blunt needles combined with electroacupuncture therapy. The selected acupoints and operating procedures were as follows: Xuehai (SP10); Liangqiu (ST34); Dubi (ST35); Neixiyan (EX‐LE4); Zusanli (ST36); Yanglingquan (GB34); Sanyinjiao (SP6); Xuanzhong (GB39). The sham acupuncture procedure involved applying blunt‐tip needles to pads attached to the acupoints, applying slight pressure to elicit a needling sensation without penetrating the skin. After simulating needle manipulation 3–5 times, the electroacupuncture device was connected, starting with a continuous wave for 5 minutes, followed by a dense‐dispersive wave for 20 minutes. The treatment was administered three times per week for 6 consecutive weeks, with a 24‐week follow‐up period after the treatment.;Experimental Comparator treatment:The electroacupuncture group received electroacupuncture treatment. The acupoint locations and operating procedures were as follows: Xuehai (SP10), perpendicular insertion 1.0 cun; Liangqiu (ST34), perpendicular insertion 1.0 cun; Dubi (ST35), oblique insertion 1.0 cun; Neixiyan (EX‐LE4), oblique insertion 1.0 cun; Zusanli (ST36), perpendicular insertion 1.2 cun; Yanglingquan (GB34), perpendicular insertion 1.0 cun; Sanyinjiao (SP6), perpendicular insertion 1.0 cun; Xuanzhong (GB39), perpendicular insertion 0.5 cun. The needles were manipulated 3–5 times. After "deqi" was achieved, the electroacupuncture device was connected, starting with a continuous wave for 5 minutes, followed by a dense‐dispersive wave for 20 minutes. Treatment frequency: three times per week for 6 consecutive weeks, with a 24‐week follow‐up period after treatment.; CONDITION: Knee Osteoarthritis PRIMARY OUTCOME: Westem Ontario and McMaster University, WOMAC; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Ultrasound of the knee joint;Inguinal lymph node ultrasound;NIR‐ICG near‐infrared detection;3D Gait Analysis;Lsokinetic muscle strength test;Knee CT;Peripheral blood metabolism/proteomics testing;Knee MRI;VAS score;Lequesne index;Six‐minute walking test;The medical outcomes study short form health survey‐36;Bone density test;Lysholm score;TCM syndrome score;Synovial fluid inflammatory factor analysis;Knee X‐ray;Blinding Success Assessment;Needle Puncture Tolerance Test; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Diagnosis of knee osteoarthritis according to the Western medicine criteria (OARSI Guidelines for the Non‐Surgical Management of Knee, Hip, and Polyarticular Osteoarthritis 2019); patients whose imaging meets the Kellgren‐Lawrence classification of grade II‐III; 2. Patients with a Lysholm swelling score; 3. Patients with knee ultrasound showing a depth of the anechoic zone of the infrapatellar fat pad greater than 3 mm; 4. Aged >=50 years and <=75 years, regardless of gender; 5. Patients who have not received acupuncture treatment within the past three months; 6. Patients with at least 6 months of knee pain, with a visual analog scale (VAS) score for knee pain greater than 4 and less than or equal to 7 during the 7 days prior to screening; 7. Understanding and consenting to participate in this study by signing an informed consent form.
