AB  -  INTERVENTION: Needle Retention Group:Filiform needles are used for acupuncture, with the even reinforcing‐reducing manipulation applied. After Deqi (the arrival of qi) is achieved, no additional operations are performed, and the needles are retained for 30 minutes.;Needle Twisting Group:Filiform needles are used for acupuncture, with the even reinforcing‐reducing manipulation applied. After Deqi (the arrival of qi) is achieved, the head acupoints including Baihui (GV20), Shenting (GV24), and Ningshen (EX‐HN16) are subjected to repeated rapid twisting along with slight lifting and thrusting. The manipulation starts slowly and accelerates gradually, with a twisting frequency of >200 times per minute, lasting for 5 minutes; the intensity is adjusted to the maximum tolerance of the patient. The total needle retention time is 30 minutes, and during this period, needle manipulation is performed once every 10 minutes. For the acupoints Dazhui (GV14), Zusanli (ST36), and Sanyinjiao (SP6), only needle retention is conducted without additional manipulation.;Group with 2 Hz:Acupuncture is performed with filiform needles, using the even reinforcing‐reducing manipulation. After deqi (the arrival of qi) is achieved, the acupoints are divided into two groups for connection to an electroacupuncture instrument: one group consists of Baihui (GV20) and Dazhui (GV14), and the other group includes Shenting (GV24) and Ningshen (Extra point). The instrument is set to a continuous wave with a frequency of 2 Hz, and the current intensity is adjusted to the maximum tolerance of the patient. The treatment duration is 30 minutes. For Zusanli (ST36) and Sanyinjiao (SP6), only needle retention is applied without connecting to the instrument.;Group with 10 Hz:The operation method is the same as that of the 2 Hz gr CONDITION: Chronic Fatigue Syndrome PRIMARY OUTCOME: Clinical Scale Evaluation; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Multimodal MRI Data;16S rDNA Sequencing Analysis and Non‐targeted Metabolomics 