AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: Intervention group: splint with electroacupuncture. Intervention 2: Intervention group: splint and tendon and nerve gliding exercises. Intervention 3: Control group: only night splint was used. CONDITION: Carpal tunnel syndrome. ; Carpal tunnel syndrome PRIMARY OUTCOME: Functional Status and Symptom Severity. Timepoint: At baseline and after the treatment (6 week). Method of measurement: Boston Carpal Tunnel Questionnaire (BCTQ) for Functional Status and Symptom Severity (BCTQ FUNCT and SYMPT). Pain severty. Timepoint: at baseline and after the treatment. Method of measurement: visual analog scale (VAS). Pinch and grip force. Timepoint: At baseline and after the treatment. Method of measurement: Using hydraulic dynamometer. ROM (flexion and extension). Timepoint: At baseline and after the treatment. Method of measurement: Inclinometer. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Mild to moderate disease stage No severe CST Lack of extreme limitation upper extremity limbs No symptoms of atrophy and muscle dystrophy Lack of other types of peripheral neuropathy No history of carpal tunnel surgery, or any damage to the median nerve The absence of autoimmune or inflammatory diseases No history of using steroid medications No use of splint or any treatment for CTS
