AB  -  INTERVENTION: acupuncture group:Acupoint selection: Lieque, Hegu, Baihui, Zusanli, Sanyinjiao, Taichong Operation method: Take bilateral acupoints, tonify and clear, leave the needle for 30 minutes after obtaining qi, and use an electroacupuncture instrument to perform sparse wave treatment in Lie Que and Zu San Li. Electroacupuncture treatment can be performed simultaneously on one or both sides, or alternatively on both sides. Three times a week, with a treatment period of two months.;Acupuncture smoking cessation device group:Using a acupuncture smoking cessation device, acupoint stimulation was performed on both sides of the column according to the instrument manual, 30 minutes per session, once a day, with the intensity limited to the maximum tolerance of the subject, and continued for 8 weeks.;Nicotine patch group:The specific dosage is based on the nicotine medication instructions, taking one tablet daily for a total of 8 weeks of treatment.; CONDITION: ICD‐10 F17.2 Tobacco dependence; tobacco addiction PRIMARY OUTCOME: Withdrawal symptoms, degree of remission of smoking cravings; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Abstinence rate;Daily smoking volume;Safety evaluation; INCLUSION CRITERIA: ? Meets the diagnostic criteria for tobacco dependence; ? Age range from 30 to 50 years old; ? Smoking age = 1 year, smoking = 10 cigarettes per day in the past 12 months; ? Exhalation carbon monoxide detection = 6ppm; ? Right handedness; ? Willing to participate in this study and sign an informed consent form.
