AB  -  INTERVENTION: Control group:On the basis of routine hypoglycemic treatment, methamphetamine tablets 0.5mg, 3 times/day orally. Follow a course of 7 days, take 4 consecutive courses. The specification of methyldiamine tablets is 0.5mg/ tablet (Approval number: Sinopol H20030812, Eisai (China) Pharmaceutical Co., LTD.).;Treatment group:On the basis of the treatment of the control group, the "Tongluo tonifying deficiency" electroacupuncture treatment was given, 30min/ time /d, 6 times for 1 course of treatment and 1 day of rest between courses, and 4 consecutive courses of intervention. Prescriptions of acupoints: Hegu (bilateral), Taichong (bilateral), Zusanli (bilateral), Sanyinjiao (bilateral), Tianshu (bilateral), Zhongwan and Guanyuan. Electroacupuncture operation: After the qi is obtained by acupuncture, the density wave is taken by electroacupuncture, the frequency is 2Hz/100Hz, the current intensity is in the range of 0.1 1.0MA (depending on the patients comfort), and the electroacupuncture stimulation is performed.; CONDITION: Diabetic peripheral neuropathy PRIMARY OUTCOME: TCM syndrome integral;TCSS nervous system integral; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Current Sensing Value Measurement (CPT); INCLUSION CRITERIA: ? It meets the clinical diagnostic criteria of DPN in this study and TCM syndrome differentiation is Yin deficiency and blood stasis type; ? Age 35‐70 years old; ? Vital signs were stable, blood pressure, heart rate and other indicators were normal; ? Normal cognitive ability and expression ability, no serious cardiovascular and cerebrovascular diseases; ? No other peripheral nervous system lesions; ? Volunteer to participate in this study and sign informed consent, can cooperate with doctors to complete clinical research.
