AB  -  INTERVENTION: Electroacupuncture group:To receive the stimulation of Tianshu electroacupuncture all needles will be twisted lifted and inserted during use for at least 30 seconds in order to achieve "qi" (including acid numbness swelling pain comprehensive feeling).Electroacupuncture parameters: The density wave of 2/100 Hz is selected and the current intensity is gradually increased until the needle vibrates slightly but does not cause discomfort to the patient. ;Sham Electroacupuncture group:Superficial skin puncture (depth of 2 to 3 mm) is performed at non‐Tianshu points, and no qi acupuncture operation is performed; The location of non‐Tianshu points is far away from the traditional Tianshu points or meridians; CONDITION: Acute lung injury due to sepsis PRIMARY OUTCOME: Oxygenation index (P/F); SECONDARY OUTCOME: Safety Indicators: Side Effects and Adverse Reactions of Electroacupuncture Treatment: Document any adverse events related to electroacupuncture.;ICU stay;28 day mortality;Chest X‐ray or CT image;Serum inflammatory factor levels;Respiratory function: lung compliance respiratory rate tidal volume mechanical ventilation time;Bronchoalveolar lavage fluid inflammatory indicators;Ventilator parameters: HR, MAP, RR and other vital signs; PaO2, PaCO2, Lac and other blood gas indicators;SOFA score and APACHE II score;Clinical Symptoms and Signs: Degree of Dyspnea: Assessed using a subjective scoring scale to evaluate the patient's level of breathlessness.;Vital Signs: Including heart rate, blood pressure, and body temperature; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Voluntarily sign informed consent; 2. Adult patients (=18 years old); 3. No gender restriction; 4. Meet the diagnostic criteria of sepsis and acute lung injury (ALI/ARDS).
