AB  -  INTERVENTION: Treatment Group:The combined treatment of electroacupuncture and Western medicine is adopted. The electroacupuncture operation is carried out by professionals who have received unified training to ensure the standardization and safety of the operation. a. Electroacupuncture treatment: Select Shenshu, Pishu, Zusanli, and Yanglingquan. Operation: A 0.25× 40mm disposable sterile filiform needle is used. The electroacupuncture frequency is 2/100Hz (alternating between dense and sparse waves), and the intensity is limited to the patients tolerance. Each time for 30 minutes, three times a week, for 12 consecutive weeks. Western medicine treatment: Oral metformin (500 mg bid) + alendronate sodium (70 mg per week. This drug should be taken upright on an empty stomach, otherwise it is easy to cause esophageal ulcers. Regularly monitor the adverse reactions of this drug). The dosage should be adjusted according to the patients tolerance. For example, when blood glucose is less than 4.0 mmol/L, the dosage of metformin should be reduced by 25%.;Control Group:Western medicine treatment: The combination of acupuncture and medication group. Pseudo‐electroacupuncture: Shallow puncture at non‐acupoints (1.5 cun away from the acupoint, 1‐3 mm shallow puncture, no current output, using non‐penetrating comfort needles (such as Streitberger needles) + simulated current patches (attached beside the acupoint, output 15Hz microcurrent to produce a tingling sensation on the skin, no therapeutic intensity). The treatment course was the same as that of the treatment group.; CONDITION: Type 2 Diabetic Osteoporosis PRIMARY OUTCOME: Bone mineral density; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Bone‐Alkaline Phosphatase,Bone‐Specific Alkaline Phosphatase,Beta CrossLaps;Glycated Hemoglobin; C‐Reactive Protein, Tumor Necrosis Factor‐alpha;TCM syndrome score;SF‐36 Quality of Life Survey; INCLUSION CRITERIA: (1) Simultaneously meet the following diagnostic criteria for both traditional Chinese and We