AB  -  INTERVENTION: Medical Device, Procedure/Surgery : 1. Intervention Name: Electroacupuncture Treatment (1 session per visit, total 2 sessions, 2Hz frequency, continuous wave, 15‐minute needling, with the current at the minimum stimulation level felt by the subject) 2. Medical Device Used: Sterilized acupuncture needles with a size of at least 0.16mm*15mm and electroacupuncture stimulator 3. Differences Between Intervention Groups: Order of acupuncture point combinations 3‐1. Intervention Group 1: Electroacupuncture treatment at bilateral Zusanli (ST‐36) and Yinlingquan (SP9) during Visit 1 ? Electroacupuncture treatment at bilateral Neiguan (PC6) and Waiguan (TE5) during Visit 2 3‐2. Intervention Group 2: Electroacupuncture treatment at bilateral Neiguan (PC6) and Waiguan (TE5) during Visit 1 ? Electroacupuncture treatment at bilateral Zusanli (ST‐36) and Yinlingquan (SP9) during Visit 2 4. Washout period : 1 week CONDITION: Neoplasms PRIMARY OUTCOME: Cancer pain intensity questionnaire SECONDARY OUTCOME: Activity data collected from the smart band Cancer pain intensity and pain characteristics questionnaire Heart rate variability (HRV) parameters collected from the heart rate variability measurement device. Pain questionnaire for the past 24 hours Pulse diagnostic parameters collected from the pulse measurement device. INCLUSION CRITERIA: The following criteria must be met for inclusion: 1) Adults aged 19 to 80 years, both male and female 2) Diagnosed with cancer stages 1 to 4 (ICD codes: C00–C97) 3) Experiencing continuous cancer pain for the past 3 months with a Numerical Rating Scale (NRS) of 4 or higher at the time of visit 4) Able to understand the purpose and procedures of this clinical trial, respond to pain questionnaires, and voluntarily sign the informed consent form
