AB  -  Objective: To observe the clinical effect of applying electroacupuncture at neck part and abdominal acupuncture to treating cervical spondylotic arteriopathy. Method: 100 cases were selected and randomly divided into two groups 50 cases of each. The treat group took abdominal acupuncture and electroacupuncture at neck part, the control group took electroacupuncture at neck part. Observe the clinical effect of two groups after a course of treatment, the improvement of clinical symptoms and following up of the clinical effect after three months after treatment. Result: Compared the total effective rate of two groups after a course of treatment, there was a significant difference(P<0.05); compared the improvement of different symptoms of two groups in the treatment, dizziness, headache and visual and audio impairments, the total effective rates of the treat group were higher than those of the control group, there were significant differences(P<0.05); compared the total effective rate of two groups after three months after treatment, there was a much significant difference(P<0.01). Conclusion: Applying electroacupuncture and abdominal acupuncture to treating cervical spondylotic arteriopathy has a satisfying effect, and advantages such as easy operation, satisfying effect, no side effect, low recurerence rate etc. So it deserves clinical extending and applying.
