AB  -  INTERVENTION: Electroacupuncture Group:The patient was placed in prone position 40min before surgery, and the acupoints Baihui, Fengchi (double), Neiguan (double), and Hegu (double) were selected. After routine disinfection, the acupuncturologist used one‐hand needle insertion and straight acupuncture, and performed flat, reinforcing and purging techniques to obtain qi. The Neiguan and Hegu points on both sides were connected respectively, and dense wave shape was selected (stimulation parameters: intensity 8±2mA, frequency 15/100Hz). To the patients tolerance, the stimulation was removed after 30 minutes.;Control Group:On the basis of conventional treatment, simulated electroacupuncture was used to perform blank control treatment. Acupuncture needles and acupoints were the same as those in the treatment group. First, the microporous medical tape is covered at the patients acupuncture points, and the acupuncture needle is placed in the hole of the medical tape (without penetrating the skin). After 1 min, the electrical stimulator is connected uniformly and powered on for 30 min without loading current.; CONDITION: acute stroke PRIMARY OUTCOME: Incidence of acute stroke; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Incidence of symptomatic stroke;Incidence of occult stroke;Incidence of cerebral vasospasm;The number of vascular dissection; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Aged 18‐75 years old, BMI < 28kg/m2; 2. ASA grade I‐III; 3. Selective intracranial aneurysm interventional surgery; 4. The patient agrees to the electroacupuncture treatment and signs the informed consent.
