AB  -  INTERVENTION: E02.186.250 Electroacupuncture at IG4 acupuncture point (Hegu) for 20 minutes. Current intensity and frequency according to the intervention used: current intensity at the sensory threshold with 10z (40 subjects), or current intensity at the sensory threshold with 100z (40 subjects), or current intensity at 10z motor threshold (40 subjects ), or current intensity at motor threshold with 100z (40 subjects), or Sham (40 subjects) Procedure/surgery CONDITION: Healthy Volunteers M01.774.500 PRIMARY OUTCOME: Cortical excitability is expected to be reduced when the parameters are in the sensory intensity, with both low (10 Hz) and high (100 Hz) frequency. Increased cortical excitability when the intensity is at the motor level, regardless of the frequency used. SECONDARY OUTCOME: Secondary outcomes are not expected INCLUSION CRITERIA: Healthy subjects aged between 18 and 45 years.
