AB  -  INTERVENTION: Procedure/Surgery : 1. Electroacupuncture and Electronic Moxibustion + Alpha blocker group ‐ Patients receive electroacupuncture and electronic moxibustion treatment 3 times a week for a total of 6 weeks. During the procedure, the patient is treated with electroacupuncture in the prone position and then with electroacupuncture and electronic moxibustion in the supine position. After exposing the treatment site properly, insert disposable sterilization needle for 15 minutes at the intensity of 16Hz using electric stimulator. Simultaneously with electroacupuncture, apply a piece of gauze and treat the electronic moxibustion for 15 minutes with a temperature stimulus of 45?. 2. Alpha blocker group ‐ Patients continue to take previously prescribed alpha blocker for si Xweeks. CONDITION: Diseases of The genitoruinary system PRIMARY OUTCOME: Total International Prostate Symptom Score(IPSS) change after 6 weeks from baseline SECONDARY OUTCOME: Average flow rate Clinical relevance (MCID ratio) Maximum flow rate Prostate volume Quality of Life(IPSS life satisfaction, EQ‐5D) Safety assessment(Adverse effect) Total International Prostate Symptom Score(IPSS) change after 3 weeks, 12 weeks from baseline INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1) Man over 50 years old and under 79 years old who is diagnosed with prostatic hyperplasia and is taking alpha blocker 2) Total International Prostate Symptom Score (Total IPSS) is 8 or more and 19 or less 3) Able and willing to comply with the intervention and follow‐up evaluation 4) Able to provide written informed consent
