AB  -  INTERVENTION: Electroacupuncture Group:(1) Acupoint Selection: Baihui (GV20), Yintang (GV29), Shenmen (HT7), and Sanyinjiao (SP6). Localization strictly followed the National Standard of the People's Republic of China: Nomenclature and Location of Acupuncture Points (GB12346‐90). (2) Procedure: Participants took a supine position. After routine disinfection, disposable sterile acupuncture needles were inserted. After achieving the Deqi sensation at all points, the needle handles of Baihui and Yintang, as well as Shenmen and Sanyinjiao, were connected to an electroacupuncture apparatus (Hwato brand, Model DZ‐IIB pulse electroacupuncture instrument, alternating current output, non‐polarized). A continuous wave was applied with a frequency of 2 Hz, stimulation setting 2‐5, and a pulse width of 0.2‐1.0 ms. The intensity was adjusted to the patients tolerance. The stimulation lasted for 30 min, after which the needles were removed. (3) Treatment Course: Once every other day, 3 times per week, for 4 weeks, totaling 12 sessions.;Sham Electroacupuncture Group:(1) Acupoint Selection: The same acupoints were selected as in the electroacupuncture group. (2) Procedure: Participants took a supine position. After routine disinfection, disposable blunt‐tipped needles were used. When the blunt tip touched the skin, the participant felt a pricking sensation, but the needle did not penetrate the skin. The needle handles of Baihui and Yintang, as well as the bilateral Shenmen and Sanyinjiao, were connected to the electroacupuncture apparatus (Hwato brand, Model SDZ‐IIB). The device was powered on, but the stimulation intensity output was kept at zero. The session lasted for 30 minutes. Afterward, the acupuncturist pressed the acupoints with a dry cotton ball to simulate the sensation of needle with CONDITION: Chronic insomnia PRIMARY OUTCOME: Non‐Rapid Eye Movement (NREM) stage beta wave power; SECONDARY OUTCOME: Sleep quality evaluation metrics monitored by PSG.;Sleep structure evaluation metrics monitored by PSG;Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Inde X(PSQI);Hyperarousal Scale (HAS);Pre‐Sleep Awakening Assessment Scale;Anxiety Self‐Rating Scale;Depression Self‐Rating Scale (SDS);Autonomic Function Scale (AFS);ECG indicators;EEG indicators;blood pressure;Norepinephrine;cortisol; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1)Meets the diagnostic criteria for Chronic Insomnia Disorder as defined by the International Classification of Sleep Disorders, Third Edition (ICSD‐3). 2)Aged between 18 and 65 years, inclusive. 3)Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Inde X(PSQI) global score > 7. 4)Not currently receiving and have not received any psychotropic medications (e.g., antidepressants, anxiolytics, hypnotics) within the [specify time frame, e.g., 4 weeks] prior to screening. 5)Able to comprehend the content of study questionnaires, cooperate with the treatment protocol, and perform basic smartphone operations without significant communication or cognitive barriers. 6)Voluntarily agrees to participate in the study, accept randomized group assignment, and has provided written informed consent.
