AB  -  INTERVENTION: ContentAI Regulation Electroacupuncture Central Regulatory Group:1.Acupuncture Point Selection: Based on the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) meridian theory and clinical experience, the main acupoints selected are Zusanli (ST36), Zhongwan (CV12), Tianshu (ST25), and Neiguan (PC6). If the patient experiences severe abdominal pain, the Gongsun (SP4) acupoint is additionally stimulated. In cases of significant nausea and vomiting, the Neiting (ST44) acupoint is added. 2.Electroacupuncture Operation: A programmable electroacupuncture device (Huathuo SZP‐610G) is used, along with 0.30mm×40mm disposable sterile acupuncture needles. After routine disinfection of the acupoints, needle insertion is performed, followed by connection to the electroacupuncture device once the "de qi" sensation is achieved. 3.AI‐Regulated System: This system consists of three modules: data collection, AI analysis, and parameter adjustment. The data collection module continuously gathers patient vital signs (heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen saturation), gastrointestinal function indicators (intra‐abdominal pressure, gastric residual volume, bowel sound frequency), inflammatory cytokine levels (TNF‐a, IL‐6, PCT), and TCM syndrome information (assessed through the TCM Four Diagnostic Methods for, blood stasis, etc., and their scores). The AI analysis module employs deep learning algorithms (LSTM, Transformer) and reinforcement learning algorithms (PPO) to analyze the collected data, predict the patients gastrointestinal function status and disease progression, and generate optimized electroacupuncture parameter adjustment plans by maximizing gastrointestinal function improvement rates and minimizing inflammatory cytokine levels. The parameter adjustment module sends adjustment inst CONDITION: Acute Gastrointestinal Dysfunction PRIMARY OUTCOME: Gastrointestinal function indicators (intra‐abdominal pressure, gastric residual volume, bowel sound frequency);Inflammation and Immune Indices;Traditional Chinese Medicine Syndrome Criteria; SECONDARY OUTCOME: 28‐day mortality rate; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Meet the diagnostic criteria of Sepsis 3.0: there is evidence of infection and the Sequential Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score is =2 points. 2. Combined with acute gastrointestinal dysfunction (AGI), meeting any of the following conditions: According to the AGI grading standard (2016 version), reaching grade II or above (risk or early manifestation of gastrointestinal dysfunction and failure). Clinical manifestations: symptoms of gastrointestinal motility disorders such as abdominal distension, vomiting, weakened or disappeared bowel sounds, increased gastric residual volume (>200 ml) lasting for = 24 hours. 3. Patients should be included in the study within 48‐72 hours after sepsis diagnosis. 4. Have not received electroacupuncture treatment or other traditional Chinese medicine interventions for gastrointestinal dysfunction. 5. Vital signs are relatively stable: systolic blood pressure =90 mmHg (or maintained with the support of vasoactive drug
