AB  -  INTERVENTION: Procedure/Surgery : Thread embedding acupuncture will be administered once a week for four weeks. 14 TEAs (Dongbang Medical, Sungnam, South Korea) of 29G X25mm[30 mm thread] will be inserted on seven acupoints on both sides. The acupoints and the type of TEA for intervention are as follows. 1. ST5?ST6: Transverse insertion from ST5 to ST6. 2. Near ST5?ST6: Transverse insertion on the horizontal line 5–10 mm from the ST5?ST6 line. 3. ST6?ST7: Transverse insertion from ST6 to ST7. 4. TE20?GB8: Transverse insertion from ST6 to ST7. 5. GB3?GB7: Transverse insertion from ST6 to ST7. 6. TE16?TE17: Transverse insertion from ST6 to ST7. 7. ST7: Oblique insertion from ST7 to the space between the zygomatic arch and mandibular notch. Physical therapy will be performed once weekly for 15 minutes for 4 weeks. TENS therapy will use current at 2 Hz and 100 Hz every 5 s for 15 min, at an intensity such that the patient feels electricity without pain. TENS electrodes will be attached to the bilateral temporal muscle, masseter muscle, and TMJ and a total of si Xspots will be stimulated. In the same area, simultaneously with TENS treatment for 15 min, IR therapy will be applied at a distance of at least 20–30 cm, with an intensity within 250 W. The TMD education will be conducted for all participants regardless of group assignment through educational materials on the cause, prevention, treatment, and self‐corrective stretching method. CONDITION: Diseases of the digestive system PRIMARY OUTCOME: 100mm Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) of average pain intensity on the temporomandibular joint in the last week SECONDARY OUTCOME: 100mm Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) of maximum pain intensity on the temporomandibular joint in the last week Adverse events Analgesic drug consumption Graded Chronic Pain version 2 Jaw Functional Limitation Scale‐20 Korean version of Beck's Depression Index Medical costs for economic evaluation Patient Global Impression of Change Quality of life (Short form‐12 healthy survey / EuroQol 5‐dimensions 5‐level) Treatment expectation Vertical TMJ opening INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1) regional pain in the unilateral or bilateral TMJ and masticatory muscles lasting >3 months intermittently or persistently 2) average pain intensity >40 mm on a 100 mm visual analogue scale (VAS) in the last week. (If the pain is on both sides, the one with the more pain 3) local pain in the jaw, temple, inner ear, or front of the ear caused by jaw movement, function, or parafunction according to the diagnostic criteria for temporomandibular disorders (DC/TMD) 4) myalgia, myofascial pain, or arthralgia identified by palpation assessment of the examiner according to the DC/TMD 5) adults aged 19–70 years who agree to participate in the clinical trial and provide written informed consent.
